msgid "Fill angle template"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2660
msgid ""
"This define the succetion of infill angle. When defined, it replaces the "
"fill_angle, and there won't be any extra 90° for each layer added, but the "
"fill_angle_increment will still be used. The first layer start with the "
"first angle. If a new pattern is used in a modifier, it will choose the "
"layer angle from the pattern as if it has started from the first layer.Empty "
"this settings to disable and recover the old behavior."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2673
msgid "Fill density"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2675
msgid ""
"Density of internal infill, expressed in the range 0% - 100%.\n"
"Set 0 to remove any sparse infill.\n"
"Note that using a value of 100% won't change the type of infill from sparse "
"to solid. If you want only solid infill, you can set the 'Solid infill every "
"X layers' (solid_infill_every_layers) to 1 instead."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2711
msgid "Sparse fill pattern"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2713
msgid ""
"Fill pattern for general low-density infill.\n"
"If you want an 'aligned' pattern, set 90° to the fill angle increment "
"setting."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2718 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6587
msgid "Grid"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2719
#: src/slic3r/GUI/Gizmos/GLGizmoFdmSupports.cpp:67
#: src/slic3r/GUI/Gizmos/GLGizmoMmuSegmentation.cpp:125
#: src/slic3r/GUI/Gizmos/GLGizmoSimplify.cpp:96
msgid "Triangles"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2720
msgid "Stars"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2721
msgid "Cubic"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2722
msgid "Line"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2724 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6498
msgid "Honeycomb"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2725
msgid "3D Honeycomb"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2726
msgid "Gyroid"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2730
msgid "Scattered Rectilinear"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2731
msgid "Adaptive Cubic"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2732
msgid "Support Cubic"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2733
msgid "Lightning"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2743
msgid ""
"You can increase this to over-extrude on the top layer if there is not "
"enough plastic to make a good fill."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2753
msgid ""
"You can increase this to over-extrude on the first layer if there is not "
"enough plastic because your bed isn't levelled.\n"
"Note: DON'T USE THIS if your only problem is bed leveling, LEVEL YOUR BED! "
"Use this setting only as last resort after all calibrations failed."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2763
msgid "XY First layer compensation"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2765
msgid ""
"The first layer will be grown / shrunk in the XY plane by the configured "
"value to compensate for the 1st layer squish aka an Elephant Foot effect. "
"(should be negative = inwards = remove area)"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2773
msgid "height in layers"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2774
msgid "XY First layer compensation height in layers"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2776
msgid ""
"The number of layers on which the elephant foot compensation will be active. "
"The first layer will be shrunk by the elephant foot compensation value, then "
"the next layers will be gradually shrunk less, up to the layer indicated by "
"this value."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2786
msgid "No collapse"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2787
msgid "XY First layer compensation: no collapse"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2789
msgid ""
"The compensations won't shrink thin areas below a threshold for the first "
"layer(s).\n"
"The layer(s) where this is activated depends on the "
"'first_layer_size_compensation_layers' setting."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2795 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7373
#: src/slic3r/GUI/Gizmos/GLGizmoCut.cpp:239
msgid "Width"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2796
msgid "Ironing width"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2799
msgid ""
"This is the width of the ironing pass, in a % of the top infill extrusion "
"width, should not be more than 50% (two times more lines, 50% overlap). It's "
"not necessary to go below 25% (four times more lines, 75% overlap). \n"
"If you have problems with your ironing process, don't forget to look at the "
"flow->above bridge flow, as this setting should be set to min 110% to let "
"you have enough plastic in the top layer. A value too low will make your "
"extruder eat the filament."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2813
msgid "Distribution"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2814
msgid "Ironing flow distribution"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2816
msgid ""
"This is the percentage of the flow that is used for the second ironing pass. "
"Typical 10-20%. Should not be higher than 20%, unless you have your top "
"extrusion width greatly superior to your nozzle width. A value too low and "
"your extruder will eat the filament. A value too high and the first pass "
"won't print well."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2828 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2840
msgid "Flow Compensation Model"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2830
msgid ""
"Flow Compensation Model, used to adjust the flow for small solid infill "
"lines. The model is a graph of flow correction factors (between 0 and 1) per "
"extrusion length (in mm).\n"
"The first point length has to be 0mm. the last point need to have a flow "
"correction of 1.\n"
"It's always disabled on the first layer, to not compromise adhesion."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2842
msgid "Length of an extrusion (mm)"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2843
msgid "Flow correction (ratio between 0 and 1)"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2844 src/slic3r/GUI/Field.cpp:2274
msgid "No values"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2846
msgid "Maximum length"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2847
msgid "Minimum ratio"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2848
msgid "Maximum ratio"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2860
msgid "First layer acceleration"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2862
msgid ""
"This is the maximum acceleration your printer will use for first layer.\n"
"If set to %, all accelerations will be reduced by that ratio.\n"
"Set zero to disable acceleration control for first layer."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2873
msgid "First object layer over raft interface"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2875
msgid ""
"This is the acceleration your printer will use for first layer of object "
"above raft interface.\n"
"If set to %, all accelerations will be reduced by that ratio.\n"
"Set zero to disable acceleration control for first layer of object above "
"raft interface."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2878 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3374
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4053 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4102
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4113 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4123
msgid "mm/s²"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2885
msgid "First layer bed temperature"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2887
msgid ""
"Heated build plate temperature for the first layer. Set zero to disable bed "
"temperature control commands in the output."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2897 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2920
msgid "First Layer"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2898
msgid "First layer width"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2900
msgid ""
"Set this to a non-zero value to set a manual extrusion width for first "
"layer. You can use this to force fatter extrudates for better adhesion. If "
"expressed as percentage (for example 140%) it will be computed over the "
"nozzle diameter of the nozzle used for the type of extrusion. If set to "
"zero, it will use the default extrusion width.If disabled, nothing is "
"changed compared to a normal layer.\n"
"You can set either 'Spacing', or 'Width'; the other will be calculated, "
"using the perimeter 'Overlap' percentages and default layer height."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2921
msgid "First layer spacing"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2923
msgid ""
"Like First layer width but spacing is the distance between two lines (as "
"they overlap a bit, it's not the same).\n"
"You can set either 'Spacing', or 'Width'; the other will be calculated, "
"using the perimeter 'Overlap' percentages and default layer height."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2939
msgid "First layer infill width"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2942
msgid ""
"Set this to a non-zero value to set a manual extrusion width for first layer "
"infill (sparse and solid). You can use this to force fatter extrudates for "
"better adhesion. If expressed as percentage (for example 140%) it will be "
"computed over the nozzle diameter of the nozzle used for the type of "
"extrusion. If set to zero, it will use the default extrusion width.If "
"disabled, the first layer width is also used for first layer infills (if "
"enabled).\n"
"You can set either 'Spacing', or 'Width'; the other will be calculated, "
"using the perimeter 'Overlap' percentages and default layer height."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2963
msgid "First layer infill spacing"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2965
msgid ""
"Like First layer infill width but spacing is the distance between two lines "
"(as they overlap a bit, it's not the same).\n"
"You can set either 'Spacing', or 'Width'; the other will be calculated, "
"using the perimeter 'Overlap' percentages and default layer height."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2980
msgid "First layer height"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2982
msgid ""
"When printing with very low layer heights, you might still want to print a "
"thicker bottom layer to improve adhesion and tolerance for non perfect build "
"plates. This can be expressed as an absolute value or as a percentage (for "
"example: 75%) over the lowest nozzle diameter used in by the object."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2995
msgid "Default first layer speed"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:2997
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"If expressed as absolute value in mm/s, this speed will be applied as a "
"maximum to all the print moves (but infill) of the first layer.\n"
"If expressed as a percentage it will scale the current speed.\n"
"Set it at 100% to remove any first layer speed modification (but for infill)."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3008
msgid "Max speed of object first layer over raft interface"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3011
msgid ""
"If expressed as absolute value in mm/s, this speed will be usedf as a max "
"over all the print moves of the first object layer above raft interface, "
"regardless of their type.\n"
"If expressed as a percentage it will scale the current speed (max 100%).\n"
"Set it at 100% to remove this speed modification."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3022
msgid "Max infill"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3023
msgid "Infill max first layer speed"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3025
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"If expressed as absolute value in mm/s, this speed will be applied as a "
"maximum for all infill print moves of the first layer.\n"
"If expressed as a percentage it will scale the current infill speed.\n"
"Set it at 100% to remove any infill first layer speed modification.\n"
"Set zero to disable (using first_layer_speed instead)."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3038
msgid "Min first layer speed"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3040
msgid ""
"Minimum speed when printing the first layer.\n"
"Set zero to disable."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3049
msgid "First layer nozzle temperature"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3051
msgid ""
"Extruder nozzle temperature for first layer. If you want to control "
"temperature manually during print, set zero to disable temperature control "
"commands in the output file."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3061
msgid "Full fan speed at layer"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3064
msgid ""
"Fan speed will be ramped up linearly from zero at layer "
"\"disable_fan_first_layers\" to maximum at layer \"full_fan_speed_layer\". "
"\"full_fan_speed_layer\" will be ignored if equal or lower than "
"\"disable_fan_first_layers\", in which case the fan will be running at "
"maximum allowed speed at layer \"disable_fan_first_layers\" + 1.\n"
"set 0 to disable"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3076
msgid "Fuzzy Skin"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3078
msgid "Fuzzy skin type."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3080
msgid "Outside walls"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3081
msgid "External walls"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3082
msgid "All walls"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3087
msgid "Fuzzy skin thickness"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3089
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"The maximum distance that each skin point can be offset (both ways), "
"measured perpendicular to the perimeter wall.\n"
"Can be a % of the nozzle diameter."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3098
msgid "Fuzzy skin point distance"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3100
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"Perimeters will be split into multiple segments by inserting Fuzzy skin "
"points. Lowering the Fuzzy skin point distance will increase the number of "
"randomly offset points on the perimeter wall.\n"
"Can be a % of the nozzle diameter."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3111
msgid "Enable Gap fill"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3113
msgid ""
"Enable gap fill algorithm. It will extrude small lines between perimeters "
"when there is not enough space for another perimeter or an infill."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3121
msgid "Gap fill acceleration"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3123
msgid ""
"This is the acceleration your printer will use for gap fills. \n"
"This can be expressed as a percentage over the perimeter acceleration.\n"
"Set zero to use perimeter acceleration for gap fills."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3249
msgid "Gap fill speed"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3252
msgid ""
"Speed for filling small gaps using short zigzag moves. Keep this reasonably "
"low to avoid too much shaking and resonance issues.\n"
"Gap fill extrusions are ignored from the automatic volumetric speed "
"computation, unless you set it to 0.\n"
"This can be expressed as a percentage (for example: 80%) over the Internal "
"Perimeter speed."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3263
msgid "Only ascii characters in gcode"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3265
msgid ""
"When printing the gcode file, replace any non-ascii character by a '_'. Can "
"be useful if the firmware or a software in a workflow doesn't support uft-8."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3271
msgid "Verbose G-code"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3273
msgid ""
"Enable this to get a commented G-code file, with each line explained by "
"descriptive text. If you print from an SD card, the additional weight of the "
"file could make your firmware slow down."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3280
msgid "Illegal characters"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3281
msgid "Illegal characters for filename"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3283
msgid ""
"All characters that are written here will be replaced by '_' when writing "
"the gcode file name.\n"
"If the first charater is '[' or '(', then this field will be considered as a "
"regexp (enter '[^a-zA-Z0-9]' to only use ascii char)."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3290
msgid "G-code flavor"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3292
msgid ""
"Some G/M-code commands, including temperature control and others, are not "
"universal. Set this option to your printer's firmware to get a compatible "
"output. The \"No extrusion\" flavor prevents Slic3r from exporting any "
"extrusion value at all."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3307
msgid "No extrusion"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3312
msgid "Label objects"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3313
msgid ""
"Selects whether labels should be exported at object boundaries and in what "
"format.\n"
"OctoPrint = comments to be consumed by OctoPrint CancelObject plugin.\n"
"Firmware = firmware specific G-code (it will be chosen based on firmware "
"flavor and it can end up to be empty).\n"
"\n"
"This settings is NOT compatible with Single Extruder Multi Material setup "
"and Wipe into Object / Wipe into Infill."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3321
msgid "OctoPrint comments"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3322
msgid "Firmware-specific"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3323
msgid "Print both"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3328
msgid "xyz decimals"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3330
msgid "Choose how many digits after the dot for xyz coordinates."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3335
msgid "Extruder decimals"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3337
msgid "Choose how many digits after the dot for extruder moves."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3342
msgid "G-code substitutions"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3343
msgid "Find / replace patterns in G-code lines and substitute them."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3348
msgid "High extruder current on filament swap"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3350
msgid ""
"It may be beneficial to increase the extruder motor current during the "
"filament exchange sequence to allow for rapid ramming feed rates and to "
"overcome resistance when loading a filament with an ugly shaped tip."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3357 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3666
msgid "Sparse"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3358
msgid "Infill acceleration"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3360
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"This is the acceleration your printer will use for Sparse infill.\n"
"Can be a % of the solid infill acceleration\n"
"Set zero to use solid infill acceleration for infill."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3372
msgid ""
"This is the acceleration your printer will use for travel moves. Set zero to "
"disable acceleration control for travel."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3380
msgid "Combine infill every"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3382
msgid ""
"This feature allows you to combine infill and speed up your print by "
"extruding thicker infill layers while preserving thin perimeters, thus "
"accuracy."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3385
msgid "Combine infill every n layers"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3391
msgid "Idle temperature"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3392
msgid ""
"Nozzle temperature when the tool is currently not used in multi-tool "
"setups.\n"
"This is only used when 'Ooze prevention' is active in Print Settings."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3404
msgid "Length of the infill anchor"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3407
msgid ""
"Connect an infill line to an internal perimeter with a short segment of an "
"additional perimeter. If expressed as percentage (example: 15%) it is "
"calculated over infill extrusion width. Slic3r tries to connect two close "
"infill lines to a short perimeter segment. If no such perimeter segment "
"shorter than infill_anchor_max is found, the infill line is connected to a "
"perimeter segment at just one side and the length of the perimeter segment "
"taken is limited to this parameter, but no longer than anchor_length_max. \n"
"Set this parameter to zero to disable anchoring perimeters connected to a "
"single infill line."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3419
msgid "0 (no open anchors)"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3420 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3444
msgid "1 mm"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3421 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3445
msgid "2 mm"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3422 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3446
msgid "5 mm"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3423 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3447
msgid "10 mm"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3424 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3448
msgid "1000 (unlimited)"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3429
msgid "Maximum length of the infill anchor"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3432
msgid ""
"Connect an infill line to an internal perimeter with a short segment of an "
"additional perimeter. If expressed as percentage (example: 15%) it is "
"calculated over infill extrusion width. Slic3r tries to connect two close "
"infill lines to a short perimeter segment. If no such perimeter segment "
"shorter than this parameter is found, the infill line is connected to a "
"perimeter segment at just one side and the length of the perimeter segment "
"taken is limited to infill_anchor, but no longer than this parameter. \n"
"If set to 0, the old algorithm for infill connection will be used, it should "
"create the same result as with 1000 & 0."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3443
msgid "0 (Simple connect)"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3453
msgid "Connection of sparse infill lines"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3455 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3470
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3485 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3516
msgid ""
"Give to the infill algorithm if the infill needs to be connected, and on "
"which perimeters Can be useful for art or with high infill/perimeter "
"overlap. The result may vary between infill types."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3459 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3474
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3489 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3505
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3520
msgid "Connected"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3460 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3475
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3490 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3506
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3521
msgid "Connected to hole perimeters"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3461 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3476
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3491 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3507
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3522
msgid "Connected to outer perimeters"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3462 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3477
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3492 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3508
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3523
msgid "Not connected"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3468
msgid "Connection of top infill lines"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3483
msgid "Connection of bottom infill lines"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3498
msgid "Connection of bridged infill lines"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3501
msgid ""
"Give to the bridge infill algorithm if the infill needs to be connected, and "
"on which perimeters. Can be useful to disconnect to reduce a little bit the "
"pressure buildup when going over the bridge's anchors."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3514
msgid "Connection of solid infill lines"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3529 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3530
msgid "Dense infill layer"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3532
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"Enables the creation of a support layer under the first solid layer. This "
"allows you to use a lower infill ratio without compromising the top quality. "
"The dense infill is laid out with a 50% infill density."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3539 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7326
msgid "Algorithm"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3540
msgid "Dense infill algorithm"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3542
msgid ""
"Choose the way the dense layer is laid out. The automatic option lets it try "
"to draw the smallest surface with only strait lines inside the sparse "
"infill. The Anchored option just slightly enlarges (by 'Default infill "
"margin') the surfaces that need a better support."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3548
msgid "Automatic"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3549
msgid "Automatic, unless full"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3550
msgid "Automatic, only for small areas"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3551
msgid "Automatic, or anchored if too big"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3552
msgid "Anchored"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3558
msgid "Infill extruder"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3560
msgid "The extruder to use when printing infill."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3566 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3587
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3601 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5929
#: src/slic3r/GUI/ConfigManipulation.cpp:314
msgid "Infill"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3567
msgid "Infill width"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3570
msgid ""
"Set this to a non-zero value to set a manual extrusion width for infill. If "
"left as zero, default extrusion width will be used if set, otherwise 1.125 x "
"nozzle diameter will be used. You may want to use fatter extrudates to speed "
"up the infill and make your parts stronger. If expressed as percentage (for "
"example 110%) it will be computed over nozzle diameter.\n"
"You can set either 'Spacing', or 'Width'; the other will be calculated, "
"using default layer height."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3588
msgid "Infill spacing change on even layers"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3590 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5932
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"Change width on every even layer (and not on odd layers like the first one) "
"for better overlap with adjacent layers and getting stringer shells. Try "
"values about +/- 0.1 with different sign.\n"
"This could be combined with extra permeters on even layers.\n"
"Works as absolute spacing or a % of the spacing.\n"
"set 0 to disable"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3602
msgid "Infill spacing"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3605
msgid ""
"Like First layer width but spacing is the distance between two lines (as "
"they overlap a bit, it's not the same).\n"
"You can set either 'Spacing', or 'Width'; the other will be calculated, "
"using default layer height."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3619
msgid "Internal Infill fan speed"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3621
msgid ""
"This fan speed is enforced during all Internal Infill moves\n"
"Set to 0 to stop the fan.\n"
"If disabled, default fan speed will be used.\n"
"Can be disabled by disable_fan_first_layers, slowed down by "
"full_fan_speed_layer and increased by low layer time."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3635
msgid "Infill before perimeters"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3637
msgid ""
"This option will switch the print order of perimeters and infill, making the "
"latter first."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3651
msgid "Infill/perimeters encroachment"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3653
msgid ""
"This setting applies an additional overlap between infill and perimeters for "
"better bonding. Theoretically this shouldn't be needed, but backlash might "
"cause gaps. If expressed as percentage (example: 15%) it is calculated over "
"perimeter extrusion width.\n"
"Don't put a value higher than 50% (of the perimeter width), as it will fuse "
"with it and follow the perimeter."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3667
msgid "Sparse infill speed"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3669
msgid ""
"Speed for printing the internal fill.\n"
"This can be expressed as a percentage (for example: 80%) over the Solid "
"Infill speed.\n"
"Set zero to use autospeed for this feature."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3680
msgid "Inherits profile"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3681
msgid "Name of the profile, from which this profile inherits."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3695
msgid "Interface shells"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3696
msgid ""
"Force the generation of solid shells between adjacent materials/volumes. "
"Useful for multi-extruder prints with translucent materials or manual "
"soluble support material."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3704
msgid "Internal bridges "
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3705
msgid "Internal bridges acceleration"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3707
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"This is the acceleration your printer will use for internal bridges. \n"
"Can be a % of the default acceleration\n"
"Set zero to use bridge acceleration for internal bridges."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3719
msgid "Extends internal bridge to infill"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3721
msgid ""
"When creating internal bridges, extends the line to the nearest internal "
"line it can use to support itself. This way, it can avoid curling up as when "
"bridges lines ends over a void."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3728
msgid "Infill bridges fan speed"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3730
msgid ""
"This fan speed is enforced during all infill bridges. It won't slow down the "
"fan if it's currently running at a higher speed.\n"
"Set to 0 to stop the fan.\n"
"If disabled, Bridge fan speed will be used.\n"
"Can be disabled by disable_fan_first_layers and increased by low layer time."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3745
msgid "Internal bridge infill threshold width"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3747
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"Minimum width for the solid infill to convert into an internal bridge "
"infill.\n"
"Can be a % of the current solid infill spacing."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3749 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5869
msgid "mm or %"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3755 src/slic3r/GUI/PresetHints.cpp:149
#: src/slic3r/GUI/PresetHints.cpp:177 src/slic3r/GUI/PresetHints.cpp:207
msgid "Internal bridges"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3756
msgid "Internal bridge speed"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3758
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"Speed for printing the bridges that support the top layer.\n"
"Can be a % of the bridge speed."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3767
msgid "Maximum width of a segmented region"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3768
msgid "Maximum width of a segmented region. Zero disables this feature."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3769 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3780
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5358 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5371
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5427
msgid "mm (zero to disable)"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3776
msgid "Interlocking depth of a segmented region"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3777
msgid ""
"Interlocking depth of a segmented region. It will be ignored if "
"\"mmu_segmented_region_max_width\" is zero or if "
"\"mmu_segmented_region_interlocking_depth\"is bigger then "
"\"mmu_segmented_region_max_width\". Zero disables this feature."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3787
msgid "Enable ironing"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3788
msgid ""
"Enable ironing of the top layers with the hot print head for smooth surface"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3795
msgid "Ironing acceleration"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3797
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"This is the acceleration your printer will use for ironing. \n"
"Can be a % of the top solid infill acceleration\n"
"Set zero or 100% to use top solid infill acceleration for ironing."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3808
msgid "Ironing angle"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3810
msgid ""
"Ironing post-process angle.\n"
"If positive, the ironing will use this angle.\n"
"If -1, it will use the fill angle.\n"
"If lower than -1, it will use the fill angle minus this angle."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3820 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3822
msgid "Ironing Type"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3824
msgid "All top surfaces"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3824
msgid "Topmost surface only"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3824
msgid "All solid surfaces"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3829
msgid "Flow rate"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3831
msgid ""
"Percent of a flow rate relative to object's normal layer height. It's the "
"percentage of the layer that will be over-extruded on top to do the ironing."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3840
msgid "Spacing between ironing lines"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3842
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"Distance between ironing lines.\n"
"Can be a % of the nozzle diameter used for ironing."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3852
msgid "Ironing speed"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3855
msgid ""
"Ironing speed. Used for the ironing pass of the ironing infill pattern, and "
"the post-process infill.\n"
"This can be expressed as a percentage (for example: 80%) over the Top Solid "
"Infill speed.\n"
"Ironing extrusions are ignored from the automatic volumetric speed "
"computation."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3867
msgid ""
"This custom code is inserted at every layer change, right after the Z move "
"and before the extruder moves to the first layer point. Note that you can "
"use placeholder variables for all Slic3r settings as well as {layer_num} and "
"{layer_z}."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3878
msgid "After extrusion type change in G-code"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3881
msgid ""
"This custom code is inserted at every extrusion type change.Note that you "
"can use placeholder variables for all Slic3r settings as well as "
"{last_extrusion_role}, {extrusion_role}, {layer_num} and {layer_z}. The "
"'extrusion_role' strings can take these string values: { Perimeter, "
"ExternalPerimeter, OverhangPerimeter, InternalInfill, SolidInfill, "
"TopSolidInfill, BridgeInfill, GapFill, Skirt, SupportMaterial, "
"SupportMaterialInterface, WipeTower, Mixed }. Mixed is only used when the "
"role of the extrusion is not unique, not exactly inside another category or "
"not known."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3903
msgid "Supports remaining times"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3906
msgid ""
"Emit something at 1 minute intervals into the G-code to let the firmware "
"show accurate remaining time."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3911
msgid "Method"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3912
msgid "Supports remaining times method"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3914
msgid ""
"M73: Emit M73 P{percent printed} R{remaining time in minutes} at 1 minute "
"intervals into the G-code to let the firmware show accurate remaining time. "
"As of now only the Prusa i3 MK3 firmware recognizes M73. Also the i3 MK3 "
"firmware supports M73 Qxx Sxx for the silent mode.\n"
"M117: Send a command to display a message to the printer, this is 'Time "
"Left .h..m..s'."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3921
msgid "M117"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3922
msgid "M73"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3923
msgid "M73 & M117"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3928
msgid "Supports stealth mode"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3930
msgid "The firmware supports stealth mode"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3935
msgid "Fan startup delay"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3938
msgid ""
"Move the fan start in the past by at least this delay (in seconds, you can "
"use decimals). It assumes infinite acceleration for this time estimation, "
"and will only take into account G1 and G0 moves.\n"
"It won't move fan comands from custom gcodes (they act as a sort of "
"'barrier').\n"
"It won't move fan comands into the start gcode if the 'only custom start "
"gcode' is activated.\n"
"Use 0 to deactivate."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3948
msgid "Fan delay only for overhangs"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3950
msgid "Will only take into account the delay for the cooling of overhangs."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3955
msgid "Supports binary G-code"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3957
msgid ""
"Enable, if the firmware supports binary G-code format (bgcode). To "
"generate .bgcode files, make sure you have binary G-code enabled in "
"Configuration->Preferences->Other."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3963
msgid "Fan KickStart time"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3965
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"Add a M106 S255 (max speed for fan) for this amount of seconds before going "
"down to the desired speed to kick-start the cooling fan.\n"
"This value is used for a 0->100% speedup, it will go down if the delta is "
"lower.\n"
"Set to 0 to deactivate."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3975
msgid "Min height for travel"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3977
msgid ""
"When an extruder travels to an object (from the start position or from an "
"object to another), the nozzle height is guaranteed to be at least at this "
"value.\n"
"It's made to ensure the nozzle won't hit clips or things you have on your "
"bed. But be careful to not put a clip in the 'convex shape' of an object.\n"
"Set to 0 to disable."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3988
msgid "How to apply limits"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3989
msgid "Purpose of Machine Limits"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:3992
msgid ""
"How to apply the Machine Limits.\n"
"* In every case, they will be used as safeguards: Even if you use a print "
"profile that sets an acceleration of 5000, if in your machine limits the "
"acceleration is 4000, the outputted gcode will use the 4000 limit.\n"
"* You can also use it as a safeguard and to have a better printing time "
"estimate.\n"
"* You can also use it as a safeguard, to have a better printing time "
"estimate and emit the limits at the begining of the gcode file, with M201 "
"M202 M203 M204 and M205 commands. If you want only to write a sub-set, "
"choose the 'for time estimate' option and write your own gcodes in the "
"custom gcode section."
msgstr ""

