msgid "Maximum acceleration when retracting"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4111
msgid ""
"Maximum acceleration when retracting.\n"
"\n"
"Not used for RepRapFirmware, which does not support it."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4120
msgid "Maximum acceleration for travel moves"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4122
msgid "Maximum acceleration for travel moves."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4129
msgid "Maximum G1 per second (Experimental)"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4131
msgid ""
"If your firmware stops while printing, it may have its gcode queue full. Set "
"this parameter to merge extrusions into bigger ones to reduce the number of "
"gcode commands the printer has to process each second.\n"
"On 8bit controlers, a value of 150 is typical.\n"
"Note that reducing your printing speed (at least for the external "
"extrusions) will reduce the number of time this will triggger and so "
"increase quality.\n"
"Disabled if set to 0."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4143
msgid "Max fan speed"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4146
msgid ""
"This setting represents the maximum speed of your fan, used when the layer "
"print time is Very short."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4156
msgid "Max layer height"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4158
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"This is the highest printable layer height for this extruder, used to cap "
"the variable layer height and support layer height. Maximum recommended "
"layer height is 75% of the extrusion width to achieve reasonable inter-layer "
"adhesion. \n"
"Can be a % of the nozzle diameter.\n"
"If disabled, layer height is limited to 75% of the nozzle diameter."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4173
msgid "Max auto-speed"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4174
msgid "Max print speed for Autospeed"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4177
msgid ""
"When setting other speed settings to 0, Slic3r will autocalculate the "
"optimal speed in order to keep constant extruder pressure. This experimental "
"setting is used to set the highest print speed you want to allow.\n"
"This can be expressed as a percentage (for example: 100%) over the machine "
"Max Feedrate for X axis."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4188
msgid "Max speed reduction"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4190
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"This setting control by how much the speed can be reduced to increase the "
"layer time. It's a maximum reduction, so a lower value makes the minimum "
"speed higher. Set to 90% if you don't want the speed to go below 10% of the "
"current speed.\n"
"Set zero to disable"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4202
msgid "Volumetric auto-speed"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4203
msgid "Maximum Volumetric print speed for Autospeed"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4205
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"This setting allows you to set the maximum flowrate for your print, and so "
"cap the desired flow rate for the autospeed algorithm. The autospeed tries "
"to keep a constant feedrate for the entire object, and so can lower the "
"volumetric speed for some features.\n"
"The autospeed is only enable on speed fields that have a value of 0. If a "
"speed field is a % of a 0 field, then it will be a % of the value it should "
"have got from the autospeed.\n"
"If this field is set to 0, then there is no autospeed nor maximum flowrate. "
"If a speed value i still set to 0, it will get the max speed allwoed by the "
"printer."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4219
msgid "Max volumetric slope positive"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4220
msgid ""
"This experimental setting is used to limit the speed of change in extrusion "
"rate for a transition from lower speed to higher speed. A value of 1.8 mm³/"
"s² ensures, that a change from the extrusion rate of 1.8 mm³/s (0.45mm "
"extrusion width, 0.2mm extrusion height, feedrate 20 mm/s) to 5.4 mm³/s "
"(feedrate 60 mm/s) will take at least 2 seconds."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4225 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4237
msgid "mm³/s²"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4231
msgid "Max volumetric slope negative"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4232
msgid ""
"This experimental setting is used to limit the speed of change in extrusion "
"rate for a transition from higher speed to lower speed. A value of 1.8 mm³/"
"s² ensures, that a change from the extrusion rate of 5.4 mm³/s (0.45 mm "
"extrusion width, 0.2 mm extrusion height, feedrate 60 mm/s) to 1.8 mm³/s "
"(feedrate 20 mm/s) will take at least 2 seconds."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4248
msgid ""
"This setting represents the base fan speed this filament needs, or at least "
"the minimum PWM your fan needs to work."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4258
msgid "Fan PWM from 0-100"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4260
msgid ""
"Set this if your printer uses control values from 0-100 instead of 0-255."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4267
msgid "Min layer height"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4269
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"This is the lowest printable layer height for this extruder and limits the "
"resolution for variable layer height. Typical values are between 0.05 mm and "
"0.1 mm.\n"
"Can be a % of the nozzle diameter."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4281
msgid "Minimum top width for infill"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4283
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"If a top surface has to be printed and it's partially covered by another "
"layer, it won't be considered at a top layer where its width is below this "
"value. This can be useful to not let the 'one perimeter on top' trigger on "
"surface that should be covered only by perimeters. This value can be a mm or "
"a % of the perimeter extrusion width.\n"
"Warning: If enabled, artifacts can be created is you have some thin features "
"on the next layer, like letters. Set this setting to 0 to remove these "
"artifacts."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4298
msgid "Min print speed"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4300
msgid "Slic3r will never scale the speed below this one."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4308
msgid "Minimal filament extrusion length"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4310
msgid ""
"Generate no less than the number of skirt loops required to consume the "
"specified amount of filament on the bottom layer. For multi-extruder "
"machines, this minimum applies to each extruder."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4319 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4320
msgid "Model rounding precision"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4322
msgid ""
"This is the rounding error of the input object. It's used to align points "
"that should be in the same line.\n"
"Set zero to disable."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4332
msgid "Configuration notes"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4334
msgid ""
"Here you can put your personal notes. This text will be added to the G-code "
"header comments."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4345
msgid ""
"This is the diameter of your extruder nozzle (for example: 0.5, 0.35 etc.)"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4352
msgid "Host Type"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4354
msgid ""
"Slic3r can upload G-code files to a printer host. This field must contain "
"the kind of the host.\n"
"PrusaLink is only available for prusa printer."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4377
msgid "Custom Print variables"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4380 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4998
msgid ""
"You can add data accessible to custom-gcode macros.\n"
"Each line can define one variable.\n"
"The format is 'variable_name=value'. the variable name should only have [a-"
"zA-Z0-9] characters or '_'.\n"
"A value that can be parsed as a int or float will be avaible as a numeric "
"value.\n"
"A value that is enclosed by double-quotes will be available as a string "
"(without the quotes)\n"
"A value that only takes values as 'true' or 'false' will be a boolean)\n"
"Every other value will be parsed as a string as-is.\n"
"Advice: before using a variable, it's safer to use the function "
"'default_XXX(variable_name, default_value)' (enclosed in bracket as it's a "
"script) in case it's not set. You can replace XXX by 'int' 'bool' 'double' "
"'string'."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4400
msgid ""
"This code is inserted each layer, when the object began to print (just after "
"the label if any). It's main advantage is when you use it as a object "
"modifer (right click on a model).\n"
"Special variables: 'layer_num','layer_z'"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4410
msgid "Only one perimeter on First layer"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4412
msgid ""
"Use only one perimeter on first layer, to give more space to the top infill "
"pattern."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4417
msgid "Only one perimeter on Top surfaces"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4419
msgid ""
"Use only one perimeter on flat top surface, to give more space to the top "
"infill pattern."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4424
msgid "Only one peri - other algo"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4426
msgid ""
"If you have some problem with the 'Only one perimeter on Top surfaces' "
"option, you can try to activate this on the problematic layer."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4432
msgid "Only retract when crossing perimeters"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4434
msgid ""
"Disables retraction when the travel path does not exceed the upper layer's "
"perimeters (and thus any ooze will probably be invisible)."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4440 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7240
msgid "Enable"
msgstr ""

#. TRN PrintSettings: Enable ooze prevention
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4442
msgid ""
"This option will drop the temperature of the inactive extruders to prevent "
"oozing."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4447
msgid "Output filename format"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4449
msgid ""
"You can use all configuration options as variables inside this template. For "
"example: {layer_height}, {fill_density} etc. You can also use {timestamp}, "
"{year}, {month}, {day}, {hour}, {minute}, {second}, {version}, "
"{input_filename}, {input_filename_base}, {default_output_extension}."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4458 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4604
msgid "Overhangs"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4459
msgid "Overhang acceleration"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4461
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"This is the acceleration your printer will use for overhangs.\n"
"Can be a % of the bridge acceleration\n"
"Set zero to to use bridge acceleration for overhangs."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4472
msgid "Bridge max length"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4474
msgid ""
"Maximum distance for bridges. If the distance is over that, it will be "
"considered as overhangs for 'overhangs_max_slope'.\n"
"If disabled, accept all distances.\n"
"Set to 0 to ignore bridges."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4485
msgid "Consider upper bridges"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4487
msgid ""
"Don't put overhangs if the area will filled in next layer by bridges.\n"
"If disabled, accept all upper layers.\n"
"Set to 0 to only consider our layer bridges."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4497 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4537
msgid "Dynamic overhang speeds"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4500
msgid ""
"This setting can only works correctly if dynamic speed is also enabled "
"(overhangs_dynamic_fan_speed).\n"
"Overhang size is expressed as a percentage of overlap of the extrusion with "
"the previous layer: 100% would be full overlap (no overhang), while 0% "
"represents full overhang (floating extrusion, bridge).\n"
"Fan speeds for overhang sizes in between are calculated via linear "
"interpolation.\n"
"If enabled, overhangs_fan_speed is disabled, as the fan speed for full "
"overhang is used."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4513
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid "Overhangs fan speed by % of overlap"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4514
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"Choose the Overhangs maximum fan speed for each percentage of overlap with "
"the layer below.If the current fan speed (from perimeter, external, of "
"default) is higher, then this setting won't slow the fan.\n"
"100% overlap is when the extrusion is fully on top of the previous layer's "
"extrusion.\n"
"0% overlap is when the extrusion centerline is at a distance of 'overhangs "
"threshold for speed'(overhangs_bridge_threshold)\n"
"from the nearest extrusion of the previous layer."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4520 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4558
msgid "overlap % with previous layer"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4521 src/slic3r/GUI/GCodeViewer.cpp:4480
#: src/slic3r/GUI/GCodeViewer.cpp:4499
msgid "Fan speed (%)"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4522
msgid "No fan speed"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4539
msgid ""
"Overhang size is expressed as a percentage of overlap of the extrusion with "
"the previous layer: 100% would be full overlap (no overhang), while 0% "
"represents full overhang (floating extrusion, bridge). Speeds for overhang "
"sizes in between are calculated via linear interpolation, as a percentage "
"between the the overhang speed and the (external) perimeter speed.\n"
"Note that the speeds generated to gcode will never exceed the max volumetric "
"speed value."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4551
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid "Overhangs speed ratio by % of overlap"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4552
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"Choose the Overhangs speed for each percentage of overlap with the layer "
"below.\n"
"The speed is a percentage ratio between overhangs speed (for 0% overlap) "
"and\n"
"perimeter / external perimeter speed (for 100% overlap).\n"
"100% overlap is when the extrusion is fully on top of the previous layer's "
"extrusion.\n"
"0% overlap is when the extrusion centerline is at a distance of 'overhangs "
"threshold for speed'\n"
"(overhangs_bridge_threshold) from the nearest extrusion of the previous "
"layer."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4559
msgid "Speed ratio (%)"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4560
msgid "Uses overhangs speed"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4575
msgid "Overhangs Perimeter fan speed"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4577
msgid ""
"This fan speed is enforced during all Overhang Perimeter moves\n"
"If disabled, the previous (perimeter) fan speed will be used.\n"
"Can be overriden by disable_fan_first_layers and increased by low layer time."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4589 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4590
msgid "Overhangs max slope"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4592
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"Maximum slope for overhangs. if at each layer, the overhangs hangs by more "
"than this value, then the geometry will be cut. It doesn't cut into detected "
"bridgeable areas.\n"
"Can be a % of the highest nozzle diameter.\n"
"Set to 0 to disable."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4605
msgid "Overhangs speed"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4607
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"Speed for printing overhangs.\n"
"Can be a % of the bridge speed.\n"
"Set zero to use autospeed for this feature."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4617 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4618
msgid "Enforce overhangs speed"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4621
msgid ""
"Set the speed of the full perimeters to the overhang speed, and also the "
"next one(s) if any.\n"
"Set to 0 to disable.\n"
"Set to 1 to set the overhang speed to the full perimeter if there is any "
"overhang detected inside it.\n"
"Set to more than 1 to also set the overhang speed to the next perimeter(s) "
"(only in classic mode)."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4625 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6152
#: src/slic3r/GUI/PresetHints.cpp:418
msgid "perimeters"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4631
msgid "'As bridge' speed threshold"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4632
msgid "Overhang bridge speed threshold"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4635
#, possible-c-format
msgid ""
"Minimum unsupported width for an extrusion to apply the bridge fan & "
"overhang speed to it.\n"
"Can be in mm or in a % of the nozzle diameter.\n"
"Can be overriden by the overhang flow threshold if its value lower than this "
"threshold.\n"
"If dynamic speed is used, then the dynamic speed will be computed between "
"0% and this threshold."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4647
msgid "'As bridge' flow threshold"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4648
msgid "Overhang bridge flow threshold"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4651
#, possible-c-format
msgid ""
"Minimum unsupported width for an extrusion to apply the overhang bridge flow "
"to it.\n"
"Can be in mm or in a % of the nozzle diameter.\n"
"If lower than the threshold for overhangs speed, then this threshold is used "
"for both.\n"
"If dynamic speed is used, and the overhangs speed threshold isn't enabled or "
"is higher than this one, then the dynamic speed will be computed between "
"0% and this threshold."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4665
msgid "Reverse on even"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4666
msgid "Overhang reversal on even layers"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4668
msgid ""
"Extrude perimeters that have an overhanging part in the reverse direction on "
"even layers (not on odd layers like the first one). This alternating pattern "
"can significantly improve steep overhangs.\n"
"!! this is a very slow algorithm !!"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4676
msgid "Reverse threshold"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4677
msgid "Overhang reversal threshold"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4679
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"Number of mm the overhang need to be for the reversal to be considered "
"useful. Can be a % of the perimeter width."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4688
msgid "No perimeters on bridge areas"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4691
msgid ""
"Experimental option to remove perimeters where there is nothing under them "
"and where a bridged infill should be better. \n"
" * Remove perimeters: remove the unsupported perimeters, leave the bridge "
"area as-is.\n"
" * Keep only bridges: remove the perimeters in the bridge areas, keep only "
"bridges that end in solid area.\n"
" * Keep bridges and overhangs: remove the unsupported perimeters, keep only "
"bridges that end in solid area, fill the rest with overhang "
"perimeters+bridges.\n"
" * Fill the voids with bridges: remove the unsupported perimeters, draw "
"bridges over the whole hole.* !! this one can escalate to problems with "
"overhangs shaped like  /\\, so you should use it only on one layer at a time "
"via the height-range modifier!\n"
"!!Computationally intensive!!. "
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4712
msgid "Filament parking position"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4713
msgid ""
"Distance of the extruder tip from the position where the filament is parked "
"when unloaded. This should match the value in printer firmware. "
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4721
msgid "Extra loading distance"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4722
msgid ""
"When set to zero, the distance the filament is moved from parking position "
"during load is exactly the same as it was moved back during unload. When "
"positive, it is loaded further,  if negative, the loading move is shorter "
"than unloading. "
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4730 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4918
msgid "Internal"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4731
msgid "Internal Perimeter acceleration"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4733
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"This is the acceleration your printer will use for internal perimeters. \n"
"Can be a % of the default acceleration\n"
"Set zero to use default acceleration for internal perimeters."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4744
msgid "Better bonding"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4745
msgid "Perimeter bonding"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4748
msgid ""
"This setting may slightly degrade the quality of your external perimeter, in "
"exchange for a better bonding between perimeters.Use it if you have great "
"difficulties with perimeter bonding, for example with high temperature "
"filaments.\n"
"This percentage is the % of overlap between perimeters, a bit like "
"perimeter_overlap and external_perimeter_overlap, but in reverse. You have "
"to set perimeter_overlap and external_perimeter_overlap to 100%, or this "
"setting has no effect. 0: no effect, 50%: half of the nozzle will be over an "
"already extruded perimeter while extruding a new one, unless it's an "
"external one).\n"
"Note: it needs the external and perimeter overlap to be at 100% and to print "
"the external perimeter first."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4765
msgid "Perimeter extruder"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4767
msgid ""
"The extruder to use when printing perimeters and brim. First extruder is 1."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4774 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4796
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4815 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4932
msgid "Perimeters"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4775
msgid "Perimeter width"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4778
msgid ""
"Set this to a non-zero value to set a manual extrusion width for perimeters. "
"You may want to use thinner extrudates to get more accurate surfaces. If "
"left zero, default extrusion width will be used if set, otherwise 1.125 x "
"nozzle diameter will be used. If expressed as percentage (for example 105%) "
"it will be computed over nozzle diameter.\n"
"You can set either 'Spacing', or 'Width'; the other will be calculated, "
"using the perimeter 'Overlap' percentages and default layer height."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4797
msgid "Perimeter spacing"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4799
msgid ""
"Like Perimeter width but spacing is the distance between two perimeter lines "
"(as they overlap a bit, it's not the same).\n"
"You can set either 'Spacing', or 'Width'; the other will be calculated, "
"using the perimeter 'Overlap' percentages and default layer height."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4816
msgid "Perimeters spacing change on even layers"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4829
msgid "Perimeter direction"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4832
msgid ""
"Default direction to print the perimeters (contours and holes): clockwise "
"(CW) or counter-clockwise (CCW)."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4843
msgid "Internal Perimeter fan speed"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4845
msgid ""
"This fan speed is enforced during all Perimeter moves\n"
"Set to 0 to stop the fan.\n"
"If disabled, default fan speed will be used.\n"
"Can be disabled by disable_fan_first_layers, slowed down by "
"full_fan_speed_layer and increased by low layer time."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4859 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4860
msgid "Perimeters loop"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4863
msgid ""
"Join the perimeters to create only one continuous extrusion without any z-"
"hop. Long inside travel (from external to holes) are not extruded to give "
"some space to the infill."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4869 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5535
msgid "Seam position"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4870
msgid "Perimeter loop seam"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4872
msgid "Position of perimeters starting points."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4881
msgid "perimeter overlap"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4882
msgid "Perimeter overlap"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4885
#, possible-c-format
msgid ""
"This setting allows you to reduce the overlap between the perimeters, to "
"reduce the impact of the perimeters' artifacts. 100% means that no gap is "
"left, and 0% means that perimeters are not touching each other anymore.\n"
"It's very experimental, please report about the usefulness. It may be "
"removed if there is no use for it."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4897
msgid "Perimeter reversal on even layers"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4899
msgid ""
"On even layers, all perimeter loops are reversed (it disables the overhang "
"reversal, so it doesn't double-reverse).That setting will likely create "
"defects on the perimeters, so it's only useful is for materials that have "
"some direction-dependent properties (stress lines)."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4907
msgid "Round corners"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4908
msgid "Round corners for perimeters"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4911
msgid ""
"Internal perimeters will go around sharp corners by turning around instead "
"of making the same sharp corner. This can help when there are visible holes "
"in sharp corners on internal perimeters.\n"
"Can incur some more processing time, and corners are a bit less sharp."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4919
msgid "Internal perimeters speed"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4921
msgid ""
"Speed for perimeters (contours, aka vertical shells).\n"
"This can be expressed as a percentage (for example: 80%) over the Default "
"speed.\n"
"Set zero to use autospeed for this feature."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4933
msgid "Perimeters count"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4935
msgid ""
"This option sets the number of perimeters to generate for each layer.\n"
"If perimeters_hole is activated, then this number is only for contour "
"perimeters.Note that if a contour perimeter encounter a hole, it will go "
"around like a hole perimeter.\n"
"Note that Slic3r may increase this number automatically when it detects "
"sloping surfaces which benefit from a higher number of perimeters if the "
"Extra Perimeters option is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4941
msgid " "
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4949
msgid "Max perimeter count for holes"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4952
msgid ""
"This option sets the number of perimeters to have over holes. Note that if a "
"hole-perimeter fuse with the contour, then it will go around like a contour "
"perimeter..\n"
"If disabled, holes will have the same number of perimeters as contour.\n"
"Note that Slic3r may increase this number automatically when it detects "
"sloping surfaces which benefit from a higher number of perimeters if the "
"Extra Perimeters option is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4958
msgid "(minimum)."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4966
msgid "Post-processing scripts"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4968
msgid ""
"If you want to process the output G-code through custom scripts, just list "
"their absolute paths here.\n"
"Separate multiple scripts with a semicolon or a line return.\n"
"!! please use '\\;' here if you want a not-line-separation ';'!!\n"
"Scripts will be passed the absolute path to the G-code file as the first "
"argument, and they can access the Slic3r config settings by reading "
"environment variables.\n"
"The script, if passed as a relative path, will also be searched from the "
"slic3r directory, the slic3r configuration directory and the user directory."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4983 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4984
msgid "Priming position"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4985
msgid ""
"Coordinates of the left front corner of the priming patch.\n"
"If set to 0,0 then the position is computed automatically."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:4995
msgid "Custom Printer variables"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5016 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5017
msgid "Minimum fan speed"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5019
msgid ""
"This setting represents the minimum fan speed (like minimum PWM) your fan "
"needs to work."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5027 src/slic3r/GUI/ConfigWizard.cpp:2246
msgid "Bed Temperature"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5029
msgid ""
"Override the temperature of the bed.\n"
"If disabled, uses the highest bed temperature from all filaments used in the "
"first layer."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5038
msgid "First Layer Bed Temperature"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5040
msgid ""
"Override the temperature of the bed while printing the first layer.\n"
"If disabled, uses the highest first layer bed temperature from all filaments "
"used in the first layer.\n"
"Set to 0 to prevent the slicer to do any first layer bed command."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5050
msgid "First Layer Temperature"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5052
msgid ""
"Override the temperature of the extruder (for the first layer). Avoid making "
"too many changes, it won't stop for cooling/heating.May only work on Height "
"range modifiers."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5061 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5353
msgid "Retraction length"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5063
msgid ""
"Override the retract_length setting from the printer config. Used for "
"calibration."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5070
msgid "Z-lift override"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5072
msgid ""
"Set the new lift-z value for this override. 0 will disable the z-lift. -& to "
"disable. May only work on Height range modifiers."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5080 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6731
msgid "Temperature"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5082
msgid ""
"Override the temperature of the extruder. Avoid making too many changes, it "
"won't stop for cooling/heating. May only work on Height range modifiers."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5091
msgid "Printer type"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5092
msgid "Type of the printer."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5098
msgid "Printer notes"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5100
msgid "You can put your notes regarding the printer here."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5108
msgid "Printer vendor"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5109
msgid "Name of the printer vendor."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5115
msgid "Printer variant"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5117
msgid ""
"Name of the printer variant. For example, the printer variants may be "
"differentiated by a nozzle diameter."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5148
msgid "Raft contact Z distance"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5150
msgid ""
"The vertical distance between object and raft. Ignored for soluble "
"interface. It uses the same type as the support z-offset type."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5158
msgid "Raft expansion"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5160
msgid "Expansion of the raft in XY plane for better stability."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5167
msgid "First layer density"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5168
msgid "Raft first layer density"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5170
msgid "Density of the first raft or support layer."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5178
msgid "First layer expansion"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5179
msgid "Raft first layer expansion"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5181
msgid ""
"Expansion of the first raft or support layer to improve adhesion to print "
"bed."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5188
msgid "Raft layers"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5190
msgid ""
"The object will be raised by this number of layers, and support material "
"will be generated under it."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5198
msgid "Raft layer height"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5200
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"Maximum layer height for the raft, after the first layer that uses the first "
"layer height, and before the interface layers.\n"
"Can be a % of the nozzle diameter\n"
"If set to 0, the support layer height will be used."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5211
msgid "Raft interface layer height"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5213
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"Maximum layer height for the raft interface.\n"
"Can be a % of the nozzle diameter\n"
"If set to 0, the support layer height will be used."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5223
msgid "Per region G-code"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5226
msgid ""
"This code is inserted when a region is starting to print something (infill, "
"perimeter, ironing). It's main advantage is when you use it as a object "
"modifer(right click on a model to add it there)\n"
"Special variables: 'layer_num','layer_z'"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5236
msgid "Slice resolution"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5238
msgid ""
"Minimum detail resolution, used to simplify the input file for speeding up "
"the slicing job and reducing memory usage. High-resolution models often "
"carry more details than printers can render. Set zero to disable any "
"simplification and use full resolution from input. \n"
"Note: Slic3r has an internal working resolution of 0.0001mm.\n"
"Infill & Thin areas are simplified up to 0.0125mm."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5264
msgid "Command buffer"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5266
msgid ""
"Buffer the firmware has for gcode comamnds. Allow to have some burst of "
"command with a rate over 'max_gcode_per_second' for a few instant."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5273
msgid "Minimum extrusion length"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5276
msgid ""
"When outputting gcode, this setting ensure that there is almost no commands "
"more than this value apart. Be sure to also use max_gcode_per_second "
"instead, as it's much better when you have very different speeds for "
"features (Too many too small commands may overload the firmware / "
"connection).\n"
"Disabled if set to 0."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5290
msgid "minimum resolution"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5293
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"Maximum deviation of exported G-code paths from their full resolution "
"counterparts when some commands are culled by 'gcode_min_length' or "
"'max_gcode_per_second' to not overload the firmware.\n"
"Can be a % of perimeter width."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5303
msgid "Internal resolution"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5305
msgid ""
"Minimum detail resolution, used for internal structures (gapfill and some "
"infill patterns).\n"
"Don't put a too-small value (0.05mm is way too low for many printers), as it "
"may create too many very small segments that may be difficult to display and "
"print."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5315
msgid "Minimum travel after retraction"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5317
msgid ""
"Retraction is not triggered when travel moves are shorter than this length."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5325
msgid "Minimum travel after z lift"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5327
msgid "Z lift is not triggered when travel moves are shorter than this length."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5335
msgid "Retract amount before wipe"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5337
msgid ""
"With bowden extruders, it may be wise to do some amount of quick retract "
"before doing the wipe movement."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5345
msgid "Retract on layer change"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5347
msgid "This flag enforces a retraction whenever a Z move is done (before it)."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5354
msgid "Retraction Length"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5356
msgid ""
"When retraction is triggered, filament is pulled back by the specified "
"amount (the length is measured on raw filament, before it enters the "
"extruder)."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5365 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5421
#: src/slic3r/GUI/Gizmos/GLGizmoMeasure.cpp:2016
msgid "Length"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5366 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5422
msgid "Retraction Length (Toolchange)"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5367 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5423
msgid ""
"When retraction is triggered before changing tool, filament is pulled back "
"by the specified amount (the length is measured on raw filament, before it "
"enters the extruder).\n"
"Note: This value will be unretracted when this extruder will load the next "
"time."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5378
msgid "Ramping slope angle"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5379
msgid ""
"Minimum slope of the ramp in the initial phase of the travel. If the travel "
"isn't long enough, the angle will be increased.\n"
"90° means a direct lift, like if there was no ramp.\n"
"0° means that the lift will always be hit at the end of the travel."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5391
msgid "Use ramping lift"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5392
msgid ""
"Generates a ramping lift instead of lifting the extruder directly upwards. "
"The travel is split into two phases: the ramp and the standard horizontal "
"travel. This option helps reduce stringing.\n"
"Also works for the z move when a layer change occurs."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5413
msgid "Steeper ramp before obstacles"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5414
msgid ""
"If enabled, PrusaSlicer detects obstacles along the travel path and makes "
"the slope steeper in case an obstacle might be hit during the initial phase "
"of the travel."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5434
msgid "Lift height"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5436
msgid ""
"If you set this to a positive value, the extruder is quickly raised every "
"time a retraction is triggered. When using multiple extruders, only the "
"setting for the first extruder will be considered."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5447
msgid "Above Z"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5448
msgid "Only lift Z above"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5450
msgid ""
"If you set this to a positive value, Z lift will only take place above the "
"specified absolute Z. You can tune this setting for skipping lift on the "
"first layers."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5458
msgid "Below Z"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5459
msgid "Only lift Z below"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5461
msgid ""
"If you set this to a positive value, Z lift will only take place below the "
"specified absolute Z. You can tune this setting for limiting lift to the "
"first layers."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5470
msgid "Enforce on first layer"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5471
msgid "Enforce lift on first layer"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5473
msgid ""
"Select this option to enforce z-lift on the first layer.\n"
"Useful to still use the lift on the first layer even if the 'Only lift Z "
"below' (retract_lift_above) is higher than 0."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5481
msgid "On surfaces"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5482
msgid "Lift only on"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5484
msgid "Select this option to not use/enforce the z-lift on a top surface."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5493
msgid "Deretraction extra length"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5494
msgid ""
"When the retraction is compensated after the travel move, the extruder will "
"push this additional amount of filament. This setting is rarely needed."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5502
msgid "Extra length on restart"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5503
msgid "Extrat length on toolchange restart"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5504
msgid ""
"When the retraction is compensated after changing tool, the extruder will "
"push this additional amount of filament (but not on the first extruder after "
"start, as it should already be loaded)."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5513 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5514
msgid "Retraction Speed"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5516
msgid "The speed for retractions (this only applies to the extruder motor)."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5524 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5525
msgid "Deretraction Speed"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5527
msgid ""
"The speed for loading of a filament into extruder after retraction (this "
"only applies to the extruder motor). If left as zero, the retraction speed "
"is used."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5537
msgid ""
"Position of perimeters' starting points.\n"
"Cost-based option let you choose the angle and travel cost. A high angle "
"cost will place the seam where it can be hidden by a corner, the travel cost "
"place the seam near the last position (often at the end of the previous "
"infill). Default is 60 % and 100 %. There is also the visibility and the "
"overhang cost, but they are static.\n"
" Scattered: seam is placed at a random position on external perimeters\n"
" Random: seam is placed at a random position for all perimeters\n"
" Aligned: seams are grouped in the best place possible (minimum 6 layers per "
"group)\n"
" Contiguous: seam is placed over a seam from the previous layer (useful with "
"enforcers)\n"
" Rear: seam is placed at the far side (highest Y coordinates)"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5548
msgid "Cost-based"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5549
msgid "Scattered"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5550
#: src/slic3r/GUI/ArrangeSettingsDialogImgui.cpp:107
#: src/slic3r/GUI/Preferences.cpp:1067
msgid "Random"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5551
msgid "Aligned"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5552
msgid "Contiguous"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5554 src/slic3r/GUI/MainFrame.cpp:1692
msgid "Rear"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5559
msgid "Angle cost"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5560
msgid "Seam angle cost"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5562
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"Cost of placing the seam at a bad angle. The worst angle (max penalty) is "
"when it's flat.\n"
"100% is the default penalty"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5571
msgid "Seam gap"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5573
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"To avoid visible seam, the extrusion can be stoppped a bit before the end of "
"the loop.\n"
"Can be a mm or a % of the current extruder diameter."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5583
msgid "Seam gap for external perimeters"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5586
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"To avoid visible seam, the extrusion can be stoppped a bit before the end of "
"the loop.\n"
" this setting is enforced only for external perimeter. It overrides "
"'seam_gap' if different than 0\n"
"Can be a mm or a % of the current seam gap."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5597
msgid "for everything"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5598
msgid "Seam notch"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5600
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"It's sometimes very problematic to have a little buldge from the seam. This "
"setting move the seam inside the part, in a little cavity (for every seams "
"in external perimeters, unless it's in an overhang).\n"
"The size of the cavity is in mm or a % of the external perimeter width. It's "
"overriden by the two other 'seam notch' setting when applicable.\n"
"Set zero to disable."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5613
msgid "max angle"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5614
msgid "Seam notch maximum angle"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5616
msgid ""
"If the (external) angle at the seam is higher than this value, then no notch "
"will be set. If the angle is too high, there isn't enough room for the "
"notch.\n"
"Can't be lower than 180° or it filters everything. At 360, it allows "
"everything."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5626
msgid "for round holes"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5627
msgid "Seam notch for round holes"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5630
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"In convex holes (circular/oval), it's sometimes very problematic to have a "
"little buldge from the seam. This setting move the seam inside the part, in "
"a little cavity (for all external perimeters in convex holes, unless it's in "
"an overhang).\n"
"The size of the cavity is in mm or a % of the external perimeter width\n"
"Set zero to disable."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5643
msgid "for round perimeters"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5644
msgid "Seam notch for round perimeters"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5647
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"In convex perimeters (circular/oval), it's sometimes very problematic to "
"have a little buldge from the seam. This setting move the seam inside the "
"part, in a little cavity (for all external perimeters if the path is convex, "
"unless it's in an overhang).\n"
"The size of the cavity is in mm or a % of the external perimeter width\n"
"Set zero to disable."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5660
msgid "Travel cost"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5661
msgid "Seam travel cost"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5663
msgid ""
"Cost of moving the extruder. The highest penalty is when the point is the "
"furthest from the position of the extruder before extruding the external "
"perimeter"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5672
msgid "use visibility check"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5673
msgid "Seam visibility check"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5675
msgid ""
"Check and penalize seams that are the most visible. launch rays to check "
"from how many direction a point is visible.\n"
"This is a compute-intensive option."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5682
msgid "Staggered inner seams"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5686
msgid ""
"This option causes the inner seams to be shifted backwards based on their "
"depth, forming a zigzag pattern."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5693
msgid "Direction"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5695
msgid "Preferred direction of the seam"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5696
msgid "Seam preferred direction"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5704
msgid "Jitter"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5706
msgid "Seam preferred direction jitter"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5707
msgid "Preferred direction of the seam - jitter"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5714
msgid "Brim"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5715
msgid "Skirt brim"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5717
msgid "Extra skirt lines on the first layer."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5718
msgid "lines"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5723
msgid "Distance from object"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5725
msgid ""
"Distance between skirt and object(s) ; or from the brim if using draft "
"shield or you set 'skirt_distance_from_brim'."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5733
msgid "from brim"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5734
msgid "Skirt distance from brim"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5736
msgid "The distance is computed from the brim and not from the objects"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5741
msgid "Skirt height"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5743
msgid ""
"Height of skirt expressed in layers. Set this to a tall value to use skirt "
"as a shield against drafts."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5751
msgid "Skirt width"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5754
msgid ""
"Horizontal width of the skirt that will be printed around each object. If "
"left as zero, first layer extrusion width will be used if set and the skirt "
"is only 1 layer height, or perimeter extrusion width will be used (using the "
"computed value if not set)."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5767
msgid "Loops (minimum)"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5768
msgid "Skirt Loops"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5770
msgid ""
"Number of loops for the skirt. If the Minimum Extrusion Length option is "
"set, the number of loops might be greater than the one configured here. Set "
"zero to disable skirt completely."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5778
msgid "Slicing Mode"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5781
msgid ""
"Use \"Even-odd\" for 3DLabPrint airplane models. Use \"Close holes\" to "
"close all holes in the model."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5783
msgid "Regular"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5783
msgid "Even-odd"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5783
msgid "Close holes"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5788
msgid "Slow down if layer print time is below"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5790
msgid ""
"If layer print time is estimated below this number of seconds, print moves "
"speed will be scaled down to extend duration to this value, if possible.\n"
"Set zero to disable."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5801
msgid "Speed"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5802
msgid "Small perimeters speed"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5805
msgid ""
"This separate setting will affect the speed of perimeters having radius <= "
"6.5mm (usually holes).\n"
"If expressed as percentage (for example: 80%) it will be calculated on the "
"Internal Perimeters speed setting above.\n"
"Set zero to disable."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5816
msgid "Min length"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5817
msgid "Min small perimeters length"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5819
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"This sets the threshold for small perimeter length. Every loop with a length "
"lower than this will be printed at small perimeter speed\n"
"Can be a mm value or a % of the nozzle diameter."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5830
msgid "Max length"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5831
msgid "Max small perimeters length"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5833
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"This sets the end of the threshold for small perimeter length. Every "
"perimeter loop lower than this will see their speed reduced a bit, from "
"their normal speed at this length down to small perimeter speed.\n"
"Can be a mm or a % of the nozzle diameter."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5845
msgid "Solid infill threshold area"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5847
msgid ""
"Force solid infill for regions having a smaller area than the specified "
"threshold."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5848 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5858
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7500
msgid "mm²"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5854
msgid "Solid infill layer threshold area"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5856
msgid ""
"Force solid infill for the whole layer when the combined area of all objects "
"that are printed at the same layer is smaller than this value."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5864
msgid "Solid infill threshold width"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5866
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"Force solid infill for parts of regions having a smaller width than the "
"specified threshold.\n"
"Can be a % of the current solid infill spacing.\n"
"Set 0 to disable."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5875
msgid "Solid infill overlap"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5877
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"This setting allows you to reduce the overlap between the lines of the solid "
"fill, to reduce the % filled if you see overextrusion signs on solid areas. "
"Note that you should be sure that your flow (filament extrusion multiplier) "
"is well calibrated and your filament max overlap is set before thinking to "
"modify this.\n"
"Note: top surfaces are still extruded with 100% overlap to prevent gaps."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5889
msgid "Solid infill extruder"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5891
msgid "The extruder to use when printing solid infill."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5897 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7441
msgid "Solid infill every"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5899
msgid ""
"This feature allows you to force a solid layer every given number of layers. "
"Zero to disable. You can set this to any value (for example 9999); Slic3r "
"will automatically choose the maximum possible number of layers to combine "
"according to nozzle diameter and layer height."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5910
msgid "Solid infill width"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5913
msgid ""
"Set this to a non-zero value to set a manual extrusion width for infill for "
"solid surfaces. If left as zero, default extrusion width will be used if "
"set, otherwise 1.125 x nozzle diameter will be used. If expressed as "
"percentage (for example 110%) it will be computed over nozzle diameter.\n"
"You can set either 'Spacing', or 'Width'; the other will be calculated, "
"using default layer height."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5930
msgid "Solid infill spacing change on even layers"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5943
msgid "Solid spacing"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5944
msgid "Solid infill spacing"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5947
msgid ""
"Like Solid infill width but spacing is the distance between two lines (as "
"they overlap a bit, it's not the same).\n"
"You can set either 'Spacing', or 'Width'; the other will be calculated, "
"using default layer height."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5961
msgid "Solid Infill fan speed"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5963
msgid ""
"This fan speed is enforced during all Solid Infill moves\n"
"Set to 0 to stop the fan.\n"
"If disabled, default fan speed will be used.\n"
"Can be disabled by disable_fan_first_layers, slowed down by "
"full_fan_speed_layer and increased by low layer time."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5977
msgid "Solid"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5978
msgid "Solid infill speed"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5980
msgid ""
"Speed for printing solid regions (top/bottom/internal horizontal shells). \n"
"This can be expressed as a percentage (for example: 80%) over the Default "
"speed.\n"
"Set zero to use autospeed for this feature."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5992
msgid "Solid layers"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:5994
msgid "Number of solid layers to generate on top and bottom surfaces."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6001 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6002
msgid "Minimum thickness of a top / bottom shell"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6010
msgid "Spiral vase"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6012
msgid ""
"This feature will raise Z gradually while printing a single-walled object in "
"order to remove any visible seam. This option requires no infill, no top "
"solid layers and no support material. You can still set any number of bottom "
"solid layers as well as skirt/brim loops. After the bottom solid layers, the "
"number of perimeters is enforce to 1.It won't work when printing more than "
"one single object."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6022
msgid "Temperature variation"
msgstr ""

#. TRN PrintSettings : "Ooze prevention" > "Temperature variation"
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6024
msgid ""
"Temperature difference to be applied when an extruder is not active. The "
"value is not used when 'idle_temperature' in filament settings is defined."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6034
msgid "Emit temperature commands automatically"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6035
msgid ""
"When enabled, Slic3r will check whether your Custom Start G-Code contains "
"M104 or M190. If so, the temperatures will not be emitted automatically so "
"you're free to customize the order of heating commands and other custom "
"actions. Note that you can use placeholder variables for all Slic3r "
"settings, so you can put a \"M109 S[first_layer_temperature]\" command "
"wherever you want.\n"
"If your Custom Start G-Code does NOT contain M104 or M190, Slic3r will "
"execute the Start G-Code after bed reached its target temperature and "
"extruder just started heating.\n"
"\n"
"When disabled, Slic3r will NOT emit commands to heat up extruder and bed, "
"leaving both to Custom Start G-Code."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6050
msgid ""
"This start procedure is inserted at the beginning, possibly prepended by "
"temperature-changing commands and others. See "
"'autoemit_temperature_commands' and 'start_gcode_manual'."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6059
msgid "Only custom Start G-code"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6062
msgid ""
"Ensure that the slicer won't add heating, fan, extruder... commands before "
"or just after your start-gcode.\n"
"If set to true, you have to write a good and complete start_gcode, as no "
"checks are made anymore.\n"
"Exemple:\n"
"G21 ; set units to millimeters\n"
"G90 ; use absolute coordinates\n"
"{if use_relative_e_distances}M83{else}M82{endif}\n"
"G92 E0 ; reset extrusion distance"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6071
msgid "Filament start G-code"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6073
msgid ""
"This start procedure is inserted at the beginning, after any printer start "
"gcode (and after any toolchange to this filament in case of multi-material "
"printers). This is used to override settings for a specific filament. If "
"Slic3r detects M104, M109, M140 or M190 in your custom codes, such commands "
"will not be prepended automatically so you're free to customize the order of "
"heating commands and other custom actions. Note that you can use placeholder "
"variables for all Slic3r settings, so you can put a \"M109 "
"S{first_layer_temperature}\" command wherever you want. If you have multiple "
"extruders, the gcode is processed in extruder order."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6090
msgid "Color change G-code"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6092
msgid ""
"This G-code will be used as a code for the color change If empty, the "
"default color change print command for the selected G-code flavor will be "
"used (if any)."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6103
msgid ""
"This G-code will be used as a code for the pause print. If empty, the "
"default pause print command for the selected G-code flavor will be used (if "
"any)."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6113
msgid "This G-code will be used as a custom code"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6121
msgid "Single Extruder Multi Material"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6123
msgid "The printer multiplexes filaments into a single hot end."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6128
msgid "Prime all printing extruders"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6130
msgid ""
"If enabled, all printing extruders will be primed at the front edge of the "
"print bed at the start of the print."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6136
msgid "Solid "
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6137
msgid "Solid acceleration"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6139
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"This is the acceleration your printer will use for solid infill. \n"
"Can be a % of the default acceleration\n"
"Set zero or 100% to use default acceleration for solid infill."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6150
msgid "No solid infill over"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6151
msgid "No solid infill over perimeters"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6156
msgid ""
"In sloping areas, when you have a number of top / bottom solid layers and "
"few perimeters,  it may be necessary to put some solid infill above/below "
"the perimeters to fulfill the top/bottom layers criteria.\n"
"By setting this to something higher than 0, you can control this behaviour, "
"which might be desirable if \n"
"undesirable solid infill is being generated on slopes.\n"
"The number set here indicates the number of layers between the inside of the "
"part and the air at and beyond which solid infill should no longer be added "
"above/below. If this setting is equal or higher than  the top/bottom solid "
"layer count, it won't do anything. If this setting is set to 1, it will "
"evict  all solid fill above/below perimeters. \n"
"Set zero to disable."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6172
msgid "Generate support material"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6174
msgid "Enable support material generation."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6180
msgid "Support acceleration"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6182
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"This is the acceleration your printer will use for support material. \n"
"Can be a % of the default acceleration\n"
"Set zero to use default acceleration for support material."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6193
msgid "Auto generated supports"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6195
msgid ""
"If checked, supports will be generated automatically based on the overhang "
"threshold value. If unchecked, supports will be generated inside the "
"\"Support Enforcer\" volumes only."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6201 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6478
msgid "Interface"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6202
msgid "Support interface acceleration"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6204
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"This is the acceleration your printer will use for support material "
"interfaces. \n"
"Can be a % of the support material acceleration\n"
"Set zero to use support acceleration for support material interfaces."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6215
msgid "XY separation between an object and its support"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6217
msgid ""
"XY separation between an object and its support. If expressed as percentage "
"(for example 50%), it will be calculated over external perimeter width."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6228 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6364
msgid "Pattern angle"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6229
msgid "Support pattern angle"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6231
msgid ""
"Use this setting to rotate the support material pattern on the horizontal "
"plane."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6239
msgid "Pattern angle swap height"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6242
msgid ""
"Use this setting to rotate the support material pattern by 90° at this "
"height (in mm). Set 0 to disable."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6249 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:8080
msgid "Support on build plate only"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6251 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:8082
msgid ""
"Only create support if it lies on a build plate. Don't create support on a "
"print."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6256 src/slic3r/GUI/Gizmos/GLGizmoCut.cpp:232
msgid "Type"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6257
msgid "Support contact distance type"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6259
msgid ""
"How to compute the vertical z-distance.\n"
"From filament: it uses the nearest bit of the filament. When a bridge is "
"extruded, it goes below the current plane.\n"
"From plane: it uses the plane-z. Same as 'from filament' if no 'bridge' is "
"extruded.\n"
"None: No z-offset. Useful for Soluble supports.\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6265
msgid "From filament"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6265
msgid "From plane"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6265
msgid "None (soluble)"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6271
msgid "Contact distance on top of supports"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6273
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"The vertical distance between support material interface and the object(when "
"the object is printed on top of the support). Setting this to 0 will also "
"prevent Slic3r from using bridge flow and speed for the first object layer. "
"Can be a % of the nozzle diameter."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6287
msgid "Contact distance under the bottom of supports"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6289
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"The vertical distance between object and support material interface(when the "
"support is printed on top of the object). Can be a % of the nozzle "
"diameter.\n"
"If set to zero, support_material_contact_distance will be used for both top "
"and bottom contact Z distances."
msgstr ""

#. TRN Print Settings: "Bottom contact Z distance". Have to be as short as possible
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6298
msgid "Same as top"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6310
msgid "Enforce support for the first"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6312
msgid ""
"Generate support material for the specified number of layers counting from "
"bottom, regardless of whether normal support material is enabled or not and "
"regardless of any angle threshold. This is useful for getting more adhesion "
"of objects having a very thin or poor footprint on the build plate."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6317
msgid "Enforce support for the first n layers"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6323
msgid "Support material extruder"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6325
msgid ""
"The extruder to use when printing support material (1+, 0 to use the current "
"extruder to minimize tool changes)."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6333
msgid "Support material width"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6336
msgid ""
"Set this to a non-zero value to set a manual extrusion width for support "
"material. If left as zero, default extrusion width will be used if set, "
"otherwise nozzle diameter will be used. If expressed as percentage (for "
"example 110%) it will be computed over nozzle diameter."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6349
msgid "Support Material fan speed"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6351
msgid ""
"This fan speed is enforced during all support moves\n"
"Set to 0 to stop the fan.\n"
"If disabled, default fan speed will be used.\n"
"Can be disabled by disable_fan_first_layers, slowed down by "
"full_fan_speed_layer."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6365
msgid "Support interface pattern angle"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6367
msgid ""
"Use this setting to rotate the support material pattern on the horizontal "
"plane.\n"
"0 to use the support_material_angle."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6376
msgid "Support interface angle increment"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6379
msgid ""
"Each layer, add this angle to the interface pattern angle. 0 to keep the "
"same angle, 90 to cross."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6387
msgid "Support interface fan speed"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6389
msgid ""
"This fan speed is enforced during all support interfaces, to be able to "
"weaken their bonding with a high fan speed.\n"
"Set to 0 to stop the fan.\n"
"If disabled, Support Material fan speed will be used.\n"
"Can only be overriden by disable_fan_first_layers."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6403
msgid "Interface loops"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6405
msgid ""
"Cover the top contact layer of the supports with loops. Disabled by default."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6410
msgid "Support material/raft interface extruder"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6412
msgid ""
"The extruder to use when printing support material interface (1+, 0 to use "
"the current extruder to minimize tool changes). This affects raft too."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6419
msgid "Top interface layers"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6421
msgid ""
"Number of interface layers to insert between the object(s) and support "
"material."
msgstr ""

#. TRN Print Settings: "Bottom interface layers". Have to be as short as possible
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6425 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6439
msgid "0 (off)"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6425 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6440
msgid "1 (light)"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6425 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6441
msgid "2 (default)"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6425 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6442
msgid "3 (heavy)"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6430
msgid "Bottom interface layers"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6432
msgid ""
"Number of interface layers to insert between the object(s) and support "
"material.\n"
"If disabled, support_material_interface_layers value is used"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6447
msgid "Closing radius"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6449
msgid ""
"For snug supports, the support regions will be merged using morphological "
"closing operation. Gaps smaller than the closing radius will be filled in."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6457
msgid "Support interface layer height"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6459
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"Maximum layer height for the support interface.\n"
"Can be a % of the nozzle diameter\n"
"If set to 0, the extruder maximum height will be used."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6469
msgid "Interface pattern spacing"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6471
msgid "Spacing between interface lines. Set zero to get a solid interface."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6479
msgid "Support interface speed"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6482
msgid ""
"Speed for printing support material interface layers.\n"
"If expressed as percentage (for example 50%) it will be calculated over "
"support material speed.\n"
"Set zero to use autospeed for this feature."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6493
msgid "Support pattern"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6495
msgid "Pattern used to generate support material."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6497
msgid "Rectilinear grid"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6503
msgid "Bottom Pattern"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6504
msgid "Support bottom interface pattern"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6506
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"Pattern for the bottom interface layers (the ones that start on the "
"object).\n"
"Default pattern is the same as the top interface, unless it's Hilbert Curve "
"or Ironing.\n"
"Note that 'Hilbert', 'Ironing' , '(filled)' patterns are really discouraged, "
"and meant to be used with soluble supports and 100% fill interface layer."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6522
msgid "Top Pattern"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6523
msgid "Support top interface pattern"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6525
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"Pattern for the top interface layers.\n"
"Note that 'Hilbert', 'Ironing' and '(filled)' patterns are meant to be used "
"with soluble supports and 100% fill interface layer."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6543
msgid "Support layer height"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6545
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"Maximum layer height for the support, after the first layer that uses the "
"first layer height, and before the interface layers.\n"
"Can be a % of the nozzle diameter\n"
"If set to 0, the extruder maximum height will be used."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6556
msgid "Pattern spacing"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6558
msgid "Spacing between support material lines."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6566
msgid "Support speed"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6568
msgid ""
"Speed for printing support material.\n"
"This can be expressed as a percentage (for example: 80%) over the Default "
"speed.\n"
"Set zero to use autospeed for this feature."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6578 src/slic3r/GUI/Gizmos/GLGizmoCut.cpp:233
#: src/slic3r/GUI/Gizmos/GLGizmoEmboss.cpp:2199
msgid "Style"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6579
msgid "Support tower style"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6581
msgid ""
"Style and shape of the support towers. Projecting the supports into a "
"regular grid will create more stable supports, while snug support towers "
"will save material and reduce object scarring.\n"
"Organic: create tree support structure, but this algorithm force to "
"synchronize the support layers with object layers, and only allow for one "
"layer height for each object."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6586
msgid "Organic"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6588
msgid "Snug"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6594
msgid "Synchronize with object layers"
msgstr ""

#. TRN PrintSettings : "Synchronize with object layers"
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6597
msgid ""
"Synchronize support layers with the object print layers. This is useful with "
"multi-material printers, where the extruder switch is expensive. This option "
"is only available when top contact Z distance is set to zero."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6604
msgid "Overhang threshold"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6606
msgid ""
"Support material will not be generated for overhangs whose slope angle (90° "
"= vertical) is above the given threshold. In other words, this value "
"represent the most horizontal slope (measured from the horizontal plane) "
"that you can print without support material. Set zero for automatic "
"detection (recommended)."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6618
msgid "With sheath around the support"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6620
msgid ""
"Add a sheath (a single perimeter line) around the base support. This makes "
"the support more reliable, but also more difficult to remove."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6626
msgid "Maximum Branch Angle"
msgstr ""

#. TRN PrintSettings: "Organic supports" > "Maximum Branch Angle"
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6629
msgid ""
"The maximum angle of the branches, when the branches have to avoid the "
"model. Use a lower angle to make them more vertical and more stable. Use a "
"higher angle to be able to have more reach."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6639
msgid "Preferred Branch Angle"
msgstr ""

#. TRN PrintSettings: "Organic supports" > "Preferred Branch Angle"
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6642
msgid ""
"The preferred angle of the branches, when they do not have to avoid the "
"model. Use a lower angle to make them more vertical and more stable. Use a "
"higher angle for branches to merge faster."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6652
msgid "Tip Diameter"
msgstr ""

#. TRN PrintSettings: "Organic supports" > "Tip Diameter"
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6655
msgid "Branch tip diameter for organic supports."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6663
msgid "Branch Diameter"
msgstr ""

#. TRN PrintSettings: "Organic supports" > "Branch Diameter"
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6666
msgid ""
"The diameter of the thinnest branches of organic support. Thicker branches "
"are more sturdy. Branches towards the base will be thicker than this."
msgstr ""

#. TRN PrintSettings: #lmFIXME
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6676
msgid "Branch Diameter Angle"
msgstr ""

#. TRN PrintSettings: "Organic supports" > "Branch Diameter Angle"
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6679
msgid ""
"The angle of the branches' diameter as they gradually become thicker towards "
"the bottom. An angle of 0 will cause the branches to have uniform thickness "
"over their length. A bit of an angle can increase stability of the organic "
"support."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6689
msgid "Branch Diameter with double walls"
msgstr ""

#. TRN PrintSettings: "Organic supports" > "Branch Diameter"
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6692
msgid ""
"Branches with area larger than the area of a circle of this diameter will be "
"printed with double walls for stability. Set this value to zero for no "
"double walls."
msgstr ""

#. TRN PrintSettings: #lmFIXME
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6706
msgid "Branch Distance"
msgstr ""

#. TRN PrintSettings: "Organic supports" > "Branch Distance"
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6709
msgid ""
"How far apart the branches need to be when they touch the model. Making this "
"distance small will cause the tree support to touch the model at more "
"points, causing better overhang but making support harder to remove."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6716
msgid "Branch Density"
msgstr ""

#. TRN PrintSettings: "Organic supports" > "Branch Density"
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6719
msgid ""
"Adjusts the density of the support structure used to generate the tips of "
"the branches. A higher value results in better overhangs but the supports "
"are harder to remove, thus it is recommended to enable top support "
"interfaces instead of a high branch density value if dense interfaces are "
"needed."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6733
msgid ""
"Extruder nozzle temperature for layers after the first one. Set zero to "
"disable temperature control commands in the output G-code."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6736
msgid "Nozzle temperature"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6744 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6745
msgid "Overlapping external perimeter"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6747
msgid ""
"Allow outermost perimeter to overlap itself to avoid the use of thin walls. "
"Note that flow isn't adjusted and so this will result in over-extruding and "
"undefined behavior.\n"
"100% means that perimeters can overlap completly on top of each other.\n"
"0% will deactivate this setting.\n"
"Values below 2% don't have any effect.\n"
"-1% will also deactivate the anti-hysteris checks for external perimeters."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6758 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6759
msgid "Overlapping all perimeters"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6761
msgid ""
"Allow all perimeters to overlap, instead of just external ones.\n"
"100% means that perimeters can overlap completly on top of each other.\n"
"0% will deactivate this setting.\n"
"Values below 2% don't have any effect.\n"
"-1% will also deactivate the anti-hysteris checks for internal perimeters."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6771 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6772
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6832
msgid "Thin walls"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6774
msgid ""
"Detect single-width walls (parts where two extrusions don't fit and we need "
"to collapse them into a single trace). If unchecked, Slic3r may try to fit "
"perimeters where it's not possible, creating some overlap leading to over-"
"extrusion."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6781
msgid "Min width"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6782
msgid "Thin walls min width"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6785
msgid ""
"Minimum width for the extrusion to be extruded (widths lower than the nozzle "
"diameter will be over-extruded at the nozzle diameter). If expressed as "
"percentage (for example 110%) it will be computed over nozzle diameter. The "
"default behavior of PrusaSlicer is with a 33% value. Put 100% to avoid any "
"sort of over-extrusion."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6796
msgid "Overlap"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6797
msgid "Thin wall overlap"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6800
msgid ""
"Overlap between the thin wall and the perimeters. Can be a % of the external "
"perimeter width (default 50%)"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6808
msgid "Merging with perimeters"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6809
msgid "Thin wall merge"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6812
msgid ""
"Allow the external perimeter to merge the thin walls in the path. You can "
"deactivate this if you are using thin walls as a custom support, to reduce "
"adhesion a little."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6818
msgid "Thin Walls"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6819
msgid "Thin walls acceleration"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6821
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"This is the acceleration your printer will use for thin walls. \n"
"Can be a % of the external perimeter acceleration\n"
"Set zero to use external perimeter acceleration for thin walls."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6833
msgid "Thin walls speed"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6836
msgid ""
"Speed for thin walls (external extrusions that are alone because the obect "
"is too thin at these places).\n"
"This can be expressed as a percentage (for example: 80%) over the External "
"Perimeter speed.\n"
"Set zero to use autospeed for this feature."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6860
msgid "Time cost"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6862
msgid ""
"This setting allows you to set how much an hour of printing time is costing "
"you in printer maintenance, loan, human albor, etc."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6865
msgid "€ per hour"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6870 src/slic3r/GUI/Tab.cpp:3701
msgid "Time estimation compensation"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6872
#, possible-c-format
msgid ""
"This setting allows you to modify the time estimation by a % amount. As "
"Slic3r only uses the Marlin algorithm, it's not precise enough if another "
"firmware is used."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6880
msgid "Time for start custom gcode"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6882
msgid ""
"This setting allows you to modify the time estimation by a flat amount to "
"compensate for start script, the homing routine, and other things."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6890
msgid "Time for toolchange"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6892
msgid ""
"This setting allows you to modify the time estimation by a flat amount for "
"each toolchange."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6902
msgid ""
"This custom code is inserted at every extruder change. If you don't leave "
"this empty, you are expected to take care of the toolchange yourself - "
"Slic3r will not output any other G-code to change the filament. You can use "
"placeholder variables for all Slic3r settings as well as {toolchange_z}, "
"{layer_z}, {layer_num}, {max_layer_z}, {previous_extruder} and "
"{next_extruder}, so e.g. the standard toolchange command can be scripted as "
"T{next_extruder}.!! Warning !!: if any character is written here, Slic3r "
"won't output any toolchange command by itself."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6915
msgid "Tool name"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6917
msgid ""
"Only used for Klipper, where you can name the extruder. If not set, will be "
"'extruderX' with 'X' replaced by the extruder number."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6924
msgid "Firmware name"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6926
msgid ""
"Used for gcode processing only (i.e. in Klipper) and has to match the "
"firmware extruder name. This parameter should generally not be changed!"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6932
msgid "Top Solid fan speed"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6934
msgid ""
"This fan speed is enforced during all top fills (including ironing).\n"
"Set to 0 to stop the fan.\n"
"If disabled, Solid Infill fan speed will be used.\n"
"Can be disabled by disable_fan_first_layers, slowed down by "
"full_fan_speed_layer."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6950
msgid ""
"Set this to a non-zero value to set a manual extrusion width for infill for "
"top surfaces. You may want to use thinner extrudates to fill all narrow "
"regions and get a smoother finish. If left as zero, default extrusion width "
"will be used if set, otherwise nozzle diameter will be used. If expressed as "
"percentage (for example 110%) it will be computed over nozzle diameter.\n"
"You can set either 'Spacing', or 'Width'; the other will be calculated, "
"using default layer height."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6966
msgid "Top solid spacing"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6969
msgid ""
"Like Top solid infill width but spacing is the distance between two lines "
"(as they overlap a bit, it's not the same).\n"
"You can set either 'Spacing', or 'Width'; the other will be calculated, "
"using default layer height."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6983
msgid "Top solid "
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6984
msgid "Top solid acceleration"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6986
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"This is the acceleration your printer will use for top solid infill. \n"
"Can be a % of the solid infill acceleration\n"
"Set zero or 100% to use solid infill acceleration for top solid infill."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6997
msgid "Top solid infill overlap"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:6999
#, possible-c-format
msgid ""
"This setting allows you to reduce the overlap between the lines of the top "
"solid fill, to reduce the % filled if you see overextrusion signs on solid "
"areas.\n"
"Note that you should be sure that your flow (filament extrusion multiplier) "
"is well calibrated and your filament max overlap is set before thinking to "
"modify this.\n"
"Also, lowering it below 100% may create visible gaps in the top surfaces\n"
"Set overlap setting is the only one that can't be reduced by the filament's "
"max overlap."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7012
msgid "Top solid"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7013
msgid "Top solid speed"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7015
msgid ""
"Speed for printing top solid layers (it only applies to the uppermost "
"external layers and not to their internal solid layers). You may want to "
"slow down this to get a nicer surface finish.\n"
"This can be expressed as a percentage (for example: 80%) over the Solid "
"Infill speed.\n"
"Set zero to use autospeed for this feature."
msgstr ""

#. TRN Print Settings: "Top solid layers"
#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7028 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7038
msgctxt "Layers"
msgid "Top"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7029
msgid "Top layers"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7031
msgid "Number of solid layers to generate on top surfaces."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7032
msgid "Top solid layers"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7040
msgid ""
"The number of top solid layers is increased above top_solid_layers if "
"necessary to satisfy minimum thickness of top shell. This is useful to "
"prevent pillowing effect when printing with variable layer height."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7043
msgid "Minimum top shell thickness"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7051
msgid "Travel acceleration"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7053
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"Acceleration for travel moves (jumps between distant extrusion points).\n"
"Can be a % of the default acceleration\n"
"Set zero to use default acceleration for travel moves."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7064
msgid "Decelerate with target acceleration"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7065
msgid "Use target acceleration for travel deceleration"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7067
msgid ""
"If selected, the deceleration of a travel will use the acceleration value of "
"the extrusion that will be printed after it (if any) "
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7074
msgid "Travel speed"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7076
msgid "Speed for travel moves (jumps between distant extrusion points)."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7084 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:12245
msgid "Is extruder used?"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7085 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:12246
msgid ""
"Vector of booleans stating whether a given extruder is used in the print."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7089
msgid "Z Travel"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7090
msgid "Z travel speed"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7092
msgid ""
"Speed for movements along the Z axis.\n"
"When set to zero, the value is ignored and regular travel speed is used "
"instead."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7101
msgid "Use firmware retraction"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7103
msgid ""
"This setting uses G10 and G11 commands to have the firmware handle the "
"retraction. Note that this has to be supported by firmware."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7109
msgid "Use relative E distances"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7111
msgid ""
"If your firmware requires relative E values, check this, otherwise leave it "
"unchecked. Most firmwares use absolute values."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7117
msgid "Use volumetric E"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7119
msgid ""
"This experimental setting uses outputs the E values in cubic millimeters "
"instead of linear millimeters. If your firmware doesn't already know "
"filament diameter(s), you can put commands like 'M200 D{filament_diameter_0} "
"T0' in your start G-code in order to turn volumetric mode on and use the "
"filament diameter associated to the filament selected in Slic3r. This is "
"only supported in recent Marlin."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7129
msgid "Enable variable layer height feature"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7131
msgid ""
"Some printers or printer setups may have difficulties printing with a "
"variable layer height. Enabled by default."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7137
msgid "Wipe while retracting"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7140
msgid ""
"This flag will move the nozzle while retracting to minimize the possible "
"blob on leaky extruders.\n"
"Note that as a wipe only happens when there is a retraction, the 'only "
"retract when crossing perimeters' print setting can greatly reduce the "
"number of wipes."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7149
msgid "Extra Wipe for external perimeters"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7150
msgid ""
"When the external perimeter loop extrusion ends, a wipe is done, going "
"slightly inside the print. The number in this settting increases the wipe by "
"moving the nozzle along the loop again before the final wipe."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7159
msgid "Wipe inside at start"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7161
msgid ""
"Before extruding an external perimeter, this flag will place the nozzle a "
"bit inward and in advance of the seam position before unretracting. It will "
"then move to the seam position before extruding."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7169
msgid "Wipe inside at end"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7172
msgid ""
"This flag will wipe the nozzle a bit inward after extruding an external "
"perimeter. The wipe_extra_perimeter is executed first, then this move inward "
"before the retraction wipe. Note that the retraction wipe will follow the "
"exact external perimeter (center) line if this parameter is disabled, and "
"will follow the inner side of the external perimeter line if enabled"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7181
msgid "Max Wipe deviation"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7182
msgid "Maximum Wipe deviation to the inside"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7184
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"By how much the 'wipe inside' can dive inside the object (if possible)?\n"
"In % of the perimeter width.\n"
"Note: don't put a value higher than 50% if you have only one perimeter, or "
"150% for two perimeter, etc... or it will ooze instead of wipe."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7194
msgid "Wipe lift"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7196
msgid ""
"When wiping, it will lift gradually to this height, so the filament can be "
"'cut' more easily.\n"
"Can be a percentage of the current layer height."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7202
msgid "Wipe lift length"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7203
msgid "Wipe length with lift"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7205
msgid ""
"Distance in the wipe that is used to lift. If higher than the wipe distance, "
"then the lift began at the start of the wipe. If lower than the wipe "
"distance, then the lift began after the start, so the end of the lift occur "
"at the end of the wipe.\n"
"Can be a percentage of the wipe distance."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7213
msgid "Minimum Wipe length"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7215
msgid ""
"Ensure the nozzle will move at least this much.\n"
"Can be a percentage of the needed travel for the retraction (if this is set "
"to 0, then it's posisble that the end of the retraction occur after the end "
"of the wipe)."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7222
msgid "Wipe only when crossing perimeters"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7225
msgid ""
"Don't wipe when you don't cross a perimeter. Need "
"'avoid_crossing_perimeters' and 'wipe' enabled."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7231
msgid "Wipe speed"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7233
msgid ""
"Speed in mm/s of the wipe. If it's faster, it will try to go further away, "
"as the wipe time is set by ( 100% - 'retract before wipe') * 'retaction "
"length' / 'retraction speed'.\n"
"If set to zero, the travel speed is used."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7241
msgid "Enable wipe tower"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7243
msgid ""
"Multi material printers may need to prime or purge extruders on tool "
"changes. Extrude the excess material into the wipe tower."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7249
msgid "Wipe Tower Speed"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7251
msgid ""
"Printing speed of the wipe tower. Capped by filament_max_volumetric_speed "
"(if set).\n"
"If set to zero, a value of 80mm/s is used."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7258
msgid "Wipe tower wipe starting speed"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7260
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"Start of the wiping speed ramp up (for wipe tower).\n"
"Can be a % of the 'Wipe tower main speed'.\n"
"Set to 0 to disable."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7268
msgid "Wipe Tower purge line width"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7270
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"When wiping, the extrusion should be at least 125% of the nozzle diameter. "
"This setting allow you to vary it, in case you need a wider one to properly "
"flush the nozzle."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7277
msgid "Purging volumes - load/unload volumes"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7278
msgid ""
"This vector saves required volumes to change from/to each tool used on the "
"wipe tower. These values are used to simplify creation of the full purging "
"volumes below. "
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7285
msgid "Purging volumes - matrix"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7286
msgid ""
"This matrix describes volumes (in cubic milimetres) required to purge the "
"new filament on the wipe tower for any given pair of tools. "
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7294
msgid "Enable advanced wiping volume"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7295
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"Allow Slic3r to compute the purge volume via smart computations. Use the "
"pigment% of each filament and following parameters"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7301
msgid "Nozzle volume"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7302
msgid ""
"The volume of melted plastic inside your nozzle. Used by 'advanced wiping'."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7303 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7321
msgid "mm3"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7308
msgid "Pigment percentage"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7309
msgid ""
"The pigment % for this filament (bewteen 0 and 1, 1=100%). 0 for translucent/"
"natural, 0.2-0.5 for white and 1 for black."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7318
msgid "Multiplier"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7319
msgid "Auto-wipe multiplier"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7320
msgid ""
"The volume multiplier used to compute the final volume to extrude by the "
"algorithm."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7327
msgid "Auto-wipe algorithm"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7328
msgid ""
"Algorithm for the advanced wipe.\n"
"Linear : volume = nozzle + volume_mult * (pigmentBefore-pigmentAfter)\n"
"Quadratic: volume = nozzle + volume_mult * (pigmentBefore-pigmentAfter)+ "
"volume_mult * (pigmentBefore-pigmentAfter)^3\n"
"Hyperbola: volume = nozzle + volume_mult * (0.5+pigmentBefore) / "
"(0.5+pigmentAfter)"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7333
#: src/slic3r/GUI/UnsavedChangesDialog.cpp:1093
msgid "Linear"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7333
msgid "Quadratric"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7333
msgid "Hyperbola"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7338
msgid "Wipe tower brim width"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7340
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"Width of the brim for the wipe tower. Can be in mm or in % of the (assumed) "
"only one nozzle diameter."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7349
msgid "No sparse layers (EXPERIMENTAL)"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7351
msgid ""
"If enabled, the wipe tower will not be printed on layers with no "
"toolchanges. On layers with a toolchange, extruder will travel downward to "
"print the wipe tower. User is responsible for ensuring there is no collision "
"with the print."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7357 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:8214
msgid "X"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7358
msgid "Wipe tower X"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7359
msgid "X coordinate of the left front corner of a wipe tower"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7365 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:8221
msgid "Y"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7366
msgid "Wipe tower Y"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7367
msgid "Y coordinate of the left front corner of a wipe tower"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7374
msgid "Wipe tower Width"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7375
msgid "Width of a wipe tower"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7381
msgid "Wipe tower rotation angle"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7382
msgid "Wipe tower rotation angle with respect to x-axis."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7388
msgid "Stabilization cone apex angle"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7389
msgid ""
"Angle at the apex of the cone that is used to stabilize the wipe tower. "
"Larger angle means wider base."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7398
msgid "Wipe tower purge lines spacing"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7399
msgid "Spacing of purge lines on the wipe tower."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7408
msgid "Wipe into this object's infill"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7409
msgid ""
"Purging after toolchange will be done inside this object's infills. This "
"lowers the amount of waste but may result in longer print time  due to "
"additional travel moves."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7417
msgid "Wipe into this object"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7418
msgid ""
"Object will be used to purge the nozzle after a toolchange to save material "
"that would otherwise end up in the wipe tower and decrease print time. "
"Colours of the objects will be mixed as a result."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7425
msgid "Maximal bridging distance"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7426
msgid "Maximal distance between supports on sparse infill sections. "
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7432
msgid "Wipe tower extruder"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7434
msgid ""
"The extruder to use when printing perimeter of the wipe tower. Set to 0 to "
"use the one that is available (non-soluble would be preferred)."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7443
msgid ""
"This feature allows to force a solid layer every given number of layers. "
"Zero to disable. You can set this to any value (for example 9999); Slic3r "
"will automatically choose the maximum possible number of layers to combine "
"according to nozzle diameter and layer height."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7453
msgid "Outer"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7454
msgid "Outer XY size compensation"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7456
msgid ""
"The object will be grown/shrunk in the XY plane by the configured value "
"(negative = inwards = remove area, positive = outwards = add area). This "
"might be useful for fine-tuning sizes.\n"
"This one only applies to the 'exterior' shell of the object.\n"
" !!! it's recommended you put the same value into the 'Inner XY size "
"compensation', unless you are sure you don't have horizontal holes. !!! "
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7467
msgid "Inner"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7468
msgid "Inner XY size compensation"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7471
msgid ""
"The object will be grown/shrunk in the XY plane by the configured value "
"(negative = inwards = remove area, positive = outwards = add area). This "
"might be useful for fine-tuning sizes.\n"
"This one only applies to the 'inner' shell of the object (!!! horizontal "
"holes break the shell !!!)"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7480
msgid "XY compensation"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7481
msgid "XY holes compensation"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7483
msgid ""
"The convex holes will be grown / shrunk in the XY plane by the configured "
"value (negative = inwards = remove area, positive = outwards = add area, "
"should be negative as the holes are always a bit smaller irl). This might be "
"useful for fine-tuning hole sizes.\n"
"This setting behaves the same as 'Inner XY size compensation' but only for "
"convex shapes. It's added to 'Inner XY size compensation', it does not "
"replace it. "
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7494
msgid "Threshold"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7495
msgid "XY holes threshold"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7497
msgid ""
"Maximum area for the hole where the hole_size_compensation will apply fully. "
"After that, it will decrease down to 0 for four times this area. Set to 0 to "
"let the hole_size_compensation apply fully for all detected holes"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7505 src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7506
msgid "Convert round holes to polyholes"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7509
msgid ""
"Search for almost-circular holes that span more than one layer and convert "
"the geometry to polyholes. Use the nozzle size and the (biggest) diameter to "
"compute the polyhole.\n"
"See http://hydraraptor.blogspot.com/2011/02/polyholes.html"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7516
msgid "Roundness margin"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7517
msgid "Polyhole detection margin"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7519
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"Maximum deflection of a point to the estimated radius of the circle.\n"
"As cylinders are often exported as triangles of varying size, points may not "
"be on the circle circumference. This setting allows you some leeway to "
"broaden the detection.\n"
"In mm or in % of the radius."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7530
msgid "Twisting"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7531
msgid "Polyhole twist"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7533
msgid "Rotate the polyhole every layer."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7538
msgid "Z offset"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7540
msgid ""
"This value will be added (or subtracted) from all the Z coordinates in the "
"output G-code. It is used to compensate for bad Z endstop position: for "
"example, if your endstop zero actually leaves the nozzle 0.3mm far from the "
"print bed, set this to -0.3 (or fix your endstop)."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7549
msgid "Z full step"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7551
msgid ""
"Set this to the height moved when your Z motor (or equivalent) turns one "
"step.If your motor needs 200 steps to move your head/platter by 1mm, this "
"field should be 1/200 = 0.005.\n"
"Note that the gcode will write the z values with 6 digits after the dot if "
"z_step is set (it's 3 digits if it's disabled).\n"
"Set zero to disable."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7564
msgid "Preferred orientation"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7566
msgid "Rotate stl around z axes while adding them to the bed."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7576
msgid "Perimeter generator"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7578
msgid ""
"Classic perimeter generator produces perimeters with constant extrusion "
"width and for very thin areas is used gap-fill. Arachne engine produces "
"perimeters with variable extrusion width. This setting also affects the "
"Concentric infill."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7582
msgid "Classic"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7582
msgid "Arachne"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7587
msgid "Perimeter transition length"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7590
msgid ""
"When transitioning between different numbers of perimeters as the part "
"becomesthinner, a certain amount of space is allotted to split or join the "
"perimeter segments. If expressed as a percentage (for example 100%), it will "
"be computed based on the nozzle diameter."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7599
msgid "Perimeter transitioning filter margin"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7601
msgid ""
"Prevent transitioning back and forth between one extra perimeter and one "
"less. This margin extends the range of extrusion widths which follow to "
"[Minimum perimeter width - margin, 2 * Minimum perimeter width + margin]. "
"Increasing this margin reduces the number of transitions, which reduces the "
"number of extrusion starts/stops and travel time. However, large extrusion "
"width variation can lead to under- or overextrusion problems.If expressed as "
"percentage (for example 25%), it will be computed over nozzle diameter."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7614
msgid "Perimeter transitioning threshold angle"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7616
msgid ""
"When to create transitions between even and odd numbers of perimeters. A "
"wedge shape with an angle greater than this setting will not have "
"transitions and no perimeters will be printed in the center to fill the "
"remaining space. Reducing this setting reduces the number and length of "
"these center perimeters, but may leave gaps or overextrude."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7627
msgid "Perimeter distribution count"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7629
msgid ""
"The number of perimeters, counted from the center, over which the variation "
"needs to be spread. Lower values mean that the outer perimeters don't change "
"in width."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7636
msgid "Minimum feature size"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7639
msgid ""
"Minimum thickness of thin features. Model features that are thinner than "
"this value will not be printed, while features thicker than the Minimum "
"feature size will be widened to the Minimum perimeter width. If expressed as "
"a percentage (for example 25%), it will be computed based on the nozzle "
"diameter."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7649
msgid "Minimum perimeter width"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7651
msgid ""
"Width of the perimeter that will replace thin features (according to the "
"Minimum feature size) of the model. If the Minimum perimeter width is "
"thinner than the thickness of the feature, the perimeter will become as "
"thick as the feature itself. If expressed as percentage (for example 85%), "
"it will be computed over nozzle diameter."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7860
msgid "Milling cutter"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7862
msgid ""
"The milling cutter to use (unless more specific extruder settings are "
"specified). "
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7880
msgid "Milling diameter"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7882
msgid "This is the diameter of your cutting tool."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7889
msgid "Tool offset"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7901
msgid "Tool z offset"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7903
msgid "."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7910
msgid "Tool z lift"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7912
msgid "Amount of lift for travel."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7918
msgid "G-Code to switch to this toolhead"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7920
msgid ""
"Put here the gcode to change the toolhead (called after the g-code "
"T{next_extruder}). You have access to {next_extruder} and "
"{previous_extruder}. next_extruder is the 'extruder number' of the new "
"milling tool, it's equal to the index (begining at 0) of the milling tool "
"plus the number of extruders. previous_extruder is the 'extruder number' of "
"the previous tool, it may be a normal extruder, if it's below the number of "
"extruders. The number of extruder is available at {extruder} and the number "
"of milling tool is available at {milling_cutter}."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7936
msgid "G-Code to switch from this toolhead"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7938
msgid ""
"Enter here the gcode to end the toolhead action, like stopping the spindle. "
"You have access to {next_extruder} and {previous_extruder}. "
"previous_extruder is the 'extruder number' of the current milling tool, it's "
"equal to the index (begining at 0) of the milling tool plus the number of "
"extruders. next_extruder is the 'extruder number' of the next tool, it may "
"be a normal extruder, if it's below the number of extruders. The number of "
"extruder is available at {extruder}and the number of milling tool is "
"available at {milling_cutter}."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7954
msgid "Milling post-processing"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7956
msgid ""
"If activated, at the end of each layer, the printer will switch to a milling "
"head and mill the external perimeters.\n"
"You should set the 'Milling extra XY size' to a value high enough to have "
"enough plastic to mill. Also, be sure that your piece is firmly glued to the "
"bed."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7964
msgid "Milling extra XY size"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7967
msgid ""
"This increases the size of the object by a certain amount to have enough "
"plastic to mill. You can set a number of mm or a percentage of the "
"calculated optimal extra width (from flow calculation)."
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7976
msgid "Milling only after"
msgstr ""

#: src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp:7978
#, possible-c-format, possible-boost-format
msgid ""
"This setting restricts the post-process milling to a certain height, to "
"avoid milling the bed. It can be a mm or a % of the first layer height (so "
"it can depend on the object)."
msgstr ""

